</div>What a bunch of panies. I am talking real, hard-core, death metal, weapons grade despair. Pages upon pages of nothing but featureless jet black.Unless the picture are of sad kittens, then it is alright.<br /> <br /> (clears throat)<br /> <br /> Right. Anyway, I don't want the &quot;New&quot; Technocracy to be the good guys, so much as another set of bad guys. I simply want them to be distinct from the Nephandi bad guys, the Maurader bad guys, and the Tradition bad guys. The Technocracts are the grind of the 9-5, gig-economy, surveillance state, Big Brother is always watching, cult of technology, Black Mirror type of people. I hope the book sticks to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T11:05:36-07:00","id":1384875,"title":"","content":"It's an M20 supplement. That means that it makes an effort to support whatever style of play the group wants. From TR: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> although many features of <b>Technocracy: Reloaded</b> remain familiar to longtime <b>Mage</b> fans, we've approached this book and its material with a broader spectrum than previous books have provided. <b>Mage 20</b>'s emphasis on Technocratic player-character options informs every aspect of this book, which provides material for players at Storytellers alike. Within that insider framework, many elements have been left deliberately ambiguous, with the final decision being left to each individual Storyteller. Depending on that Storyteller's desires, then, the current Technocracy may be:<br /> <br /> \u2022 A fine idea gone horribly wrong.<br /> \u2022 An archaic empire crumbling under its own obsolescence.<br /> \u2022 A flawed but necessary bulwark against a world filled with monsters.<br /> \u2022 A monstrous paranormal Empire with genocide all tendencies and great PR.<br /> \u2022 An implacable engine of global domination where in a few idealists struggle with in a totalitarian system.<br /> \u2022 An icon of paranoia where in a wrong move or word might lead to Fates far worse than death.<br /> \u2022 A vast, corrupt conspiracy in which good principles justify horrendous acts.<br /> \u2022 An extremist Juggernaut at war within itself.<br /> \u2022 A Titanic pawn in a Nephandic endgame.<br /> \u2022 The last, best hope for human survival.<br /> <br /> These possibilities are not, of course, mutually exclusive. </div> </div> </div>So no, it's not going to stick to the Union being an unalloyed evil; though there's plenty in the book that you can use to make that so if you so choose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T12:19:12-07:00","id":1384891,"title":"","content":"My own hopes for the M20 line is that it will last long enough for us to get books like <b>Technocracy: Reloaded</b> for the Traditions and for the Disparates (\u201cTraditions Reborn\u201d and \u201cDisparates Unbound\u201d, maybe?), and a book like <i>Book of the Fallen</i> for the Marauders (for historical reasons, \u201cBook of Madness, M20 Edition\u201d). <br /> <br /> The difference being that <b>TR</b> is designed with the notion that the game's protagonists may be from the faction under discussion, and so is sympathetic with their worldview\u00b9 and doubles as a sort of Player's Guide; whereas <b>Book of the Fallen</b> is designed as a sort of \u201cBlack Dog\u201d game where the faction under discussion is <i>in no way</i> intended to be player characters and is mostly there to facilitate a discussion about a disturbing topic (\u201cabuse\u201d in the case of the Nephandi; \u201cmental illness\u201d in the case of the Marauders) and to equip not just the player characters but also the <i>players</i> to know what they're looking at when they see it and to deal with it appropriately\u00b2.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">\u00b9 Which is <i>not</i> to say that their worldview is embraced wholeheartedly; I fully expect that if we get an equivalent book for the Traditions, their flaws and failings will receive plenty of attention, too.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">\u00b2 And the first thing that I'd want the hypothetical M20 Book of Madness to address is \u201cwhat is a mental illness, vs. what is merely a mind that works differently than the societal norm?\u201d</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-30-2020, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T12:55:00-07:00","id":1384899,"title":"","content":"Travis Legge just said in the 'Story Told' podcast that for Mage 20 books he'd like to write, a Book of Madness that distinguishes between mental illness and reality melting is something he'd like to do. Satyros Phil Brucato has mentioned a desire to do more with Marauders, but had similar concerns about making sure mental illness was a topic handled in a mature manner.<br /> <br /> So, I'd expect that if Technocracy Reloaded delivers well, Onyx Path would want to send proposals to White Wolf to do more M20 faction books. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T13:13:09-07:00","id":1384904,"title":"","content":"Well, seeing as how Technocracy Reloaded was funded in about 45 minutes and is well on its way to quadrupling the initial funding goals on day three, it will take a severe setback for it not to perform extraordinarily well overall.<br /> <br /> I just hope that Paradox is open to more M20 books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-30-2020, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T13:48:28-07:00","id":1384914,"title":"","content":"Very excited about this. I was nervous based on some statements early on but my fears have been abated. This is exactly what I wanted out of this book and I can't wait to see what they say about the updates to Iteration X in particular.<br /> <br /> It sounds like we're getting more factions for some Conventions and I'm hoping that's for Iteration X and Progenitors both in particular given they were the two that needed them the most. Glad to see those groups are getting written by someone with a scientific background no less","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T15:05:01-07:00","id":1384930,"title":"","content":"Looks like we are well on our way to Digital web 3.0.2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T17:13:26-07:00","id":1384962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1384891#post1384891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own hopes for the M20 line is that it will last long enough for us to get books like <b>Technocracy: Reloaded</b> for the Traditions and for the Disparates (\u201cTraditions Reborn\u201d and \u201cDisparates Unbound\u201d, maybe?), and a book like <i>Book of the Fallen</i> for the Marauders (for historical reasons, \u201cBook of Madness, M20 Edition\u201d).</div> </div> </div> </div>...yeah about that.<br /> <br /> So a few times in his interviews in Mage: the Podcast, Brucato revealed that he did indeed try to pitch a &quot;Guide to the Disparates&quot; book...but that pitch apparently got rejected by Paradox. And there's no way of knowing if the success of this KS would reverse their decision.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T11:09:12-07:00","id":1385093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1384930#post1384930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like we are well on our way to Digital web 3.0.2</div> </div> </div> </div>...and we have!<br /> <br /> Next up at $131,000 the Technomancer's Toolbox 20 chapter also increases in size with some notes from Q Division.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T12:19:58-07:00","id":1385108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1384962#post1384962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Brucato revealed that he did indeed try to pitch a &quot;Guide to the Disparates&quot; book...</div> </div> </div> </div>A pitch for the disparates but not for, say, the Traditions? The main playable faction?<br /> <br /> It's says a lot about the disparates being nothing more than Brucato's pet faction<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T12:29:18-07:00","id":1385115,"title":"","content":"Either that, or the fact that the Traditions have already been covered as the primary protagonist of 3 editions of the game plus getting a Guide To The Traditions, not to mention two editions worth of individual tradition books for all of them, pretty much means that there's not as much need for a Traditions Reborn book.<br /> <br /> Not to say that I wouldn't want one, just that the Disparates are far more sparse in terms of the sourcebooks covering them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T12:41:25-07:00","id":1385119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1385115#post1385115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either that, or the fact that the Traditions have already been covered as the primary protagonist of 3 editions of the game plus getting a Guide To The Traditions, not to mention two editions worth of individual tradition books for all of them, pretty much means that there's not as much need for a Traditions Reborn book.<br /> <br /> Not to say that I wouldn't want one, just that the Disparates are far more sparse in terms of the sourcebooks covering them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Yet the technocracy is getting a Reloaded edition while having been covered in 3 editions and getting a guide to the Technocracy and two editions worth of conventions books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T12:42:49-07:00","id":1385121,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> Well, the Traditions are the main characters in the game and got both a 1e or 2e book and the books in the Revised Era.<br /> <br /> Book of Crafts, which was where many of the Disparates come from, is quite dated and had several crafts that weren't brought over (likely because they were problematic). Even if Brucato's a pro-Disparate author, the Disparates are more in need of an update to make them playable in 2020 than the Traditions are.<br /> <br /> Though if Book of Crafts is just Brucato's pet faction, we are less likely to get that book than one in which other authors can do substantial work on.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1197_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1197\" data-vbnamecard=\"1197\">Imthestein</a> I also appreciate that we have some of the Technocracy sections being written by someone with a scientific background. That's one reason I really liked GURPS Biotech in its first iteration. The author was a genetic scientist and having a Biology degree, I could understand the terminology and theory they were putting in there. The Progenitors do better than being more than the mad biological scientists creating clones in the 1990s. In the 1990s, well I remember first getting to do stuff with DNA in class and the work the Human Genome Project was going to do. The Mage books of the time didn't really have sophisticated explanations of gene therapy and other technologies--they were still science fiction.<br /> <br /> Update #10 had a nice little excerpt on Terranorming and Attunement. I especially liked the part about attunement use of werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T12:48:10-07:00","id":1385122,"title":"","content":"Also, with the Technocracy and Traditions being the two main antagonists, it helps to have a Technocracy book with plenty of detail for playing the 'bad guys.' How much a game book is for those who are a player and how much is for the Storyteller depends on the writer, but it seems in M20 there's not a move to divide game participants so specifically into player and Storyteller. It's more of 'the Storyteller has different responsibilities and needs more on this stuff' than a clear divide between the participant types.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T12:57:48-07:00","id":1385125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1385122#post1385122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, with the Technocracy and Traditions being the two main antagonists, it helps to have a Technocracy book with plenty of detail for playing the 'bad guys.' How much a game book is for those who are a player and how much is for the Storyteller depends on the writer, but it seems in M20 there's not a move to divide game participants so specifically into player and Storyteller. It's more of 'the Storyteller has different responsibilities and needs more on this stuff' than a clear divide between the participant types.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That book already exist. It's called Guide to the Technocracy. It gave both details on Technocracy as antagonist or as playable faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T13:25:43-07:00","id":1385130,"title":"","content":"And we have the Revised Edition's Convention Books, most of which were written the year prior to M20 being announced. So yeah, there is something to be said for the Disparates needing an update even more than the Technocracy did. But that doesn't mean that the reasoning is as simplistic as \u201cBrucato likes the Disparates more than the Traditions\u201d. I can see that being one of the contributing factors, and I can see the dearth of material on the Disparates being another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T02:30:20-07:00","id":1385218,"title":"","content":"From various podcasts and posts it seems like Paradox isn't going to greenlight any more *20 projects for any lines. So hopefully we get a whole bunch of stretchgoals for this and hopefully Victorian Mage still goes ahead. Though Satyros has said he's looking into getting non-greenlit projects up on the Storytellers Vault just as the C20 Developers and Freelancers have done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T04:11:49-07:00","id":1385230,"title":"","content":"That Kickstarter pitch seems <i>really</i> heavy on a framing of &quot;all the dumb dumbs in the world messed everything up, and now it's time for the smart Technocracy to pull up their sleeves and clean up everybody's messes&quot;.<br /> <br /> It mentions global warming as a threat that they need to deal with, I wonder if the book will have anything to say about the Technocracy's complicity in that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T09:00:02-07:00","id":1385248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1385218#post1385218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From various podcasts and posts it seems like Paradox isn't going to greenlight any more *20 projects for any lines. So hopefully we get a whole bunch of stretchgoals for this and hopefully Victorian Mage still goes ahead. Though Satyros has said he's looking into getting non-greenlit projects up on the Storytellers Vault just as the C20 Developers and Freelancers have done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well this is news to me, but then I dont keep up with Paradox's plans or Developer interviews. Also a bit sad, I'd love to see the M20 line continue for at least a few more years.<br /> <br /> That being said, other than really (REALLY) wanting to get my hands on some Victorian Mage this Technocracy book pretty much ends the list of *required* updates needed to run my M20 games into the next decade without problems. Now don't get me wrong, I'll buy everything they make, that's a given, but actually must have for my stories, not so much. <br /> <br /> My issue is that if the M20 line is ended then what's instore for Mage Ascension fans in the future. Now I know absolutely nothing about marketing or anything like that but I would think that if a project like Technocracy Reloded, which is a supplement and not a new game in it's own right, can push to the $200,000 + mark from a Kickstarter in 30 days that it's a good sign that the market is profitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T09:37:01-07:00","id":1385256,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping that Onyx Path can negotiate the rights to develop M5 the way that Modipheus got the rights to V5 \u2014 not because I'm much of a fan of the 5th edition games (V5 didn't impress me), but because if the only way to go forward from here beyond what is already in the pipeline for M20 is to get on board the 5th Edition bandwagon then I want a company that I trust to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T05:13:43-07:00","id":1385388,"title":"","content":"Add me to the &quot;concerned that the response to 'people want to play the evil, literally-backed-the-Nazis group as heroes' is 'let's reboot them as heroes'&quot; list, although some of the fiction snippets have helped mitigate my concerns. I'm not against painting the Union in finer shades than the cartoonish villainy of ye olde 1e and giving room for individual Technocrats for being heroes... but, well, one game line over we've got a book about playing the scions of a world-spanning, world-plundering empire of elemental supersoldiers that makes no bones about <i>empires suck</i>.<br /> <br /> I don't really see why the organization that has, traditionally, been used as the face of The Man, of global corporatism, the worst bits of capitalism, the boot that stomps on a human face forever... needs apologetics about how, no, seriously, they aren't <i>that</i> bad. If you wanna be an Awakened Scientist, you've got, like, two entire traditions and a miscellany of them strewn throughout the others. (There's a surprising number of technomages in the Hermetics, in my eyes. Their science isn't the science the Technocracy would like, but even so...)<br /> <br /> <i>With that said</i>, and so I don't seem like I'm just being negative - I'm not at all against stuff like we got in Revised, where the head honchos of the Union had their control disrupted, giving more latitude for the Earth-side personnel to look around and have their <i>&quot;are we the baddies?</i>&quot; moments. I'm certainly not wanting a return to the oh-so-90s versions of Mage where all technology and science was suspect and bad, except for the <i>cool</i> science that the young people who write Mage back then liked. I merely caution that <i>maybe</i>, at this point in time, a book about how &quot;The Man&quot; isn't really that bad, the system works, it's keeping us safe is <i>remarkably</i> tone-deaf.<br /> <br /> And I really, really hope that isn't the way Technocracy Reloaded is going. I've put up my five bucks to look over the previews as they come out, but I haven't seen enough to make up my mind, yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T07:09:51-07:00","id":1385400,"title":"","content":"The thing about making an edition that's designed to cater to the Storyteller's preference is that you don't get to dictate what that preference will be. <br /> <br /> With that said, the tone I've been getting from the manuscript so far has <i>not</i> been letting the Technocracy off the hook for anything. There has been acknowledgement after acknowledgement that the Union has done terrible things in the past and continues to do terrible things even today. So I have no concerns that the book will end up being tone-deaf. <br /> <br /> As for the phenomenon of people wanting to play Technocrats: for me at least, that has never been a case of wanting to play The Man; rather, it's been more a matter of not having adequate alternatives available. Basically: if you like the way Science and Technology is handled where the Union is concerned and you don't consider the \u201clet's abandon Occam's Razor\u201d Etherites or the \u201cborderline-mystical worship of Information\u201d VAs as adequate alternatives, then the Technocracy is the only option open to you. <br /> <br /> (Well, M20 also now gives you the option to be an independent Technologist who can have precisely the view on Science and Technology that you want without having any affiliation with the faction that's set on world domination. But <i>that</i> comes with the drawback that you don't have any colleagues to speak of. <br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to Unit 8, because from what I'm seeing that's where you'll find material supporting a splinter group from the Union that's rejecting its Technocratic elements: a new faction that lets you keep the Science and Technology focus that the Union has had a near-monopoly on up until now <i>without</i> requiring you to be affiliated with its political ambitions or alternatively going it alone. And <i>that</i> lets the Storyteller take the Union itself back to being an Antagonist faction the way the Nephandi and Marauders are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T19:22:26-07:00","id":1385513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1384962#post1384962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...yeah about that.<br /> <br /> So a few times in his interviews in Mage: the Podcast, Brucato revealed that he did indeed try to pitch a &quot;Guide to the Disparates&quot; book...but that pitch apparently got rejected by Paradox. And there's no way of knowing if the success of this KS would reverse their decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if Brucato could be talked into publishing some of his ideas on STV; there are a number of potential recruits mentioned in the Disparate Alliance section of M20 that sadly are almost completely lacking in even basic information about them \u2014 just one-line blurbs that are next to useless: the Balamob, the Thunder Society, the Uzoma, Navalon (though TR may end up covering them), the Mirainohmen, the Red Thorn Dedicants, the Itz'at, and the Go Kamisori Gama. I'd buy a PDF consisting solely of two-page write-ups for each of these akin to the write-ups that the Ahl-i-Batin, Bata'a, Children of Knowledge, Hollow Ones, Kopa Loei, Ngoma, Orphans, Sisters of Hypollyta, Taft\u00e2ni, Templar Knights, and Wu Lung each get in M20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T19:34:59-07:00","id":1385516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1385513#post1385513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Brucato could be talked into publishing some of his ideas on STV; there are a number of potential recruits mentioned in the Disparate Alliance section of M20 that sadly are almost completely lacking in even basic information about them \u2014 just one-line blurbs that are next to useless: the Balamob, the Thunder Society, the Uzoma, Navalon (though TR may end up covering them), the Mirainohmen, the Red Thorn Dedicants, the Itz'at, and the Go Kamisori Gama. I'd buy a PDF consisting solely of two-page write-ups for each of these akin to the write-ups that the Ahl-i-Batin, Bata'a, Children of Knowledge, Hollow Ones, Kopa Loei, Ngoma, Orphans, Sisters of Hypollyta, Taft\u00e2ni, Templar Knights, and Wu Lung each get in M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, on the MtP Discord, M20 freelancer James H Sambrano revealed that he and Brucato were at least discussing the idea of putting what would have been in GttD onto STVault. But time will tell on that front...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T20:32:10-07:00","id":1385527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1385400#post1385400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about making an edition that's designed to cater to the Storyteller's preference is that you don't get to dictate what that preference will be.<br /> <br /> With that said, the tone I've been getting from the manuscript so far has <i>not</i> been letting the Technocracy off the hook for anything. There has been acknowledgement after acknowledgement that the Union has done terrible things in the past and continues to do terrible things even today. So I have no concerns that the book will end up being tone-deaf.<br /> <br /> <b>As for the phenomenon of people wanting to play Technocrats: for me at least, that has never been a case of wanting to play The Man; rather, it's been more a matter of not having adequate alternatives available. Basically: if you like the way Science and Technology is handled where the Union is concerned and you don't consider the \u201clet's abandon Occam's Razor\u201d Etherites or the \u201cborderline-mystical worship of Information\u201d VAs as adequate alternatives, then the Technocracy is the only option open to you.</b><br /> <br /> (Well, M20 also now gives you the option to be an independent Technologist who can have precisely the view on Science and Technology that you want without having any affiliation with the faction that's set on world domination. But <i>that</i> comes with the drawback that you don't have any colleagues to speak of.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to Unit 8, because from what I'm seeing that's where you'll find material supporting a splinter group from the Union that's rejecting its Technocratic elements: a new faction that lets you keep the Science and Technology focus that the Union has had a near-monopoly on up until now <i>without</i> requiring you to be affiliated with its political ambitions or alternatively going it alone. And <i>that</i> lets the Storyteller take the Union itself back to being an Antagonist faction the way the Nephandi and Marauders are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really?<br /> <br /> That's NEVER been my experience. I've had a lot of trouble playing the Traditions but have NEVER had trouble playing the Union. Every game is about playing the Men in Black.<br /> <br /> Mirror shades<br /> Fascism<br /> Genocide of supernaturals<br /> Moral compromises<br /> Memory wipes<br /> Betrayal<br /> Lies<br /> Brainwashing<br /> <br /> It's about playing one part Illuminati, one part X-Files, and one part megacorp supersoldier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T20:49:42-07:00","id":1385529,"title":"","content":"I do wonder how they\u2019ll present the NWO in particular on the question of \u201cGlobalism\u201d vs \u201cNationalism\u201d. The Union has in past presentations leaned heavily toward internationalism (or Western neoimperialism masquerading as internationalism, depending on your viewpoint), but that was against the backdrop of a post-Cold War neoliberal reality that H Bush literally called the \u201cNew World Order\u201d (que the right wing conspiracy theories about UN black helicopters the Technocracy is largely inspired by).<br /> <br /> Today that international order is crumbling before neonationalism, so the real world context has completely changed. There are a lot of ways this could play out in-game (ideally without casting authoritarian neonationalism as a Tradition victory and potential good thing).<br /> <br /> - The Union is losing control of the modernist world they helped build. This can correspond nicely with how establishment conservative interests like the Kochs lost control of the movement they helped build to the fringe interests they mainstreamed (such as the example of someone who actually believes Fox News and InfoWars fed conspiracy theories, rather than just benefiting from other people believing them, being elected President and taking over the Republican Party).<br /> <br /> - The Union is as comfortable with nationalism as they are with internationalism, it\u2019s all a game of mirrors to exert influence and distract from what is \u201creally going on\u201d to them.<br /> <br /> - The Union has its own nationalist factions that are now in ascent over the internationalist old guard either in reaction to sleeper politics, or because of political fallout from Control being cut off, if one is using the Revised setting.<br /> <br /> - The Union comfortably knows internationalism is inevitable thanks to technological and economic reality. The neonationalist political resurgence being witnessed are the deaththrows of the nation state. The Union can comfortably try to harness and wield these movements (to the extent that is ever possible) to block the creation of international democratic institutions, and thus assure that the inevitable tide toward internationalism favors authoritarian corporate interest instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T03:53:32-07:00","id":1385572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1385529#post1385529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder how they\u2019ll present the NWO in particular on the question of \u201cGlobalism\u201d vs \u201cNationalism\u201d. The Union has in past presentations leaned heavily toward internationalism (or Western neoimperialism masquerading as internationalism, depending on your viewpoint), but that was against the backdrop of a post-Cold War neoliberal reality that H Bush literally called the \u201cNew World Order\u201d (que the right wing conspiracy theories about UN black helicopters the Technocracy is largely inspired by).<br /> <br /> Today that international order is crumbling before neonationalism, so the real world context has completely changed. There are a lot of ways this could play out in-game (ideally without casting authoritarian neonationalism as a Tradition victory and potential good thing).</div> </div> </div> </div>I share your interest in how they will present this. Though I would argue the shift hasn't been one in which international order is crumbling or even separate from the original intentions of the Technocracy for a few reasons. First, that would presume that previous iterations of global governance operated under the desire for, or even achieved, some sort of stability. Instead, contemporary moves towards internationalism have always relied on the tools of the empire and colony--dispossession of Indigenous peoples, occupation of soveriegn nations, and the political/economic destabilization of the other to maintain the supremacy (and stability) of the metropole or colonists (within the settler nation state). For example, the imperialist moves China has made in Africa have coincided with its internal moves towards ethnoracial nationalism a la prison camps for Uyghurs. So it seems strange to separate their tools of conflict from their goals of stability since they are both often used and desired jointly and interchangeably. <br /> <br /> Second, while previous champions for this system (e.g., U.S., U.K.) are seeing new waves of ethnoracial nationalism rhetoric in the public discourse and national politics I would hardly say that they have given up their global perspectives on the empire or colony. Instead, these moves towards nationalism have been to support internally consistent rules of governance (e.g., Racial contractarianism) to ensure the capacity of the nation state to act globally as per usual (Mills, 1997). We are just seeing the truth of the relation between nationalism and the empire (i.e., Yes, U.S. elected a black president, but it is, and always has been, a white enthnoracial settler colonial nation state and it is more than happy to oppress people within its borders or help others oppress people elsewhere to ensure that). Yes, I'm aware of your parenthetical statement, but my words here seek to resist attempts at reducing real systems that hurt real bodies to viewpoints (I'm not saying this was your intent).<br /> <br /> Lastly, I would argue that taking an imperialist or colonialist understanding of reality actually allows for the tensions we see between contemporary reality and the philosophies of the technocracy to be reconciled. Specifically, I have always seen the Technocracy as operating under a system in which the dominant political (i.e., NWO) and economic (i.e., the Syndicate) realities of the world are clearly understood to be inexplicably linked to the dominant cosmologies (i.e., Void Engineers) and epistemologies (i.e., Progenitors and Iteration X). While individual Technocrats may not agree with the action of one convention they would be lying to themselves and others if they said they can't see how they are complicit--they are mages after all. So the only way they could perceive themselves as noble scientists, industrious technologists, or champions of liberal democracy is if they were operating under the same blinders as we all do, but only magnified and reified. The colorblindness of the Union is a perfect example of this. The NWO (and to an extent the greater Union) is so caught up in the magical symbolism of mutually, modernity, and progress that even in their attempt to address their participation in racism they actually fall whole ass into it. The NWO would argue that because they truly understand reality they can look past racism, but in that process they reveal their inability to see the fictional causal relations that have been made real as per the racecraft (Fields &amp; Fields, 2012). This ignorance to how systems of imperial and colonial control operate isn't a failure in their logics, but merely an indication of their reliance on systems that demand epistemological blindness. Namely, modernity and postmodernity both require ignorance of ongoing dispossession, occupation, and violence to keep going. Coloniality as we understand it was co-developed in loving embrace with modernity, not in spite of it (Mignolo, 2011). Even when they attempt to take responsibility for their actions, the Technocracy neglects to take any steps towards addressing them (e.g., rematriating Indigenous lands, ending economic exploitation) because doing so would disrupt their internal theories of reality (even if they are built on fairytale and dead bodies). By not making these moves, the Technocracy reveals that instead of being agents of objectivity or reason they are in fact hyperreal agents of the historical relations of our reality. It seems like the only Convention that gets it is the Syndicate--not surprisingly. They openly admit that their paradigms are built on magical logics of death, disposession, and exploitation (i.e., calling their agents Magic Men). I wouldnt be surprised if redlining wasn't one of their creations or maybe its the reverese. <br /> <br /> Let's also not forget that the Virtual Adepts and Society of Ether were totally fine with imperialism and colonialism until it came home to roost. So, as we are wondering how we can play moral or ethical champions of modernity, science and technology, maybe we just shouldn't worry because those fantasies are built upon fantasies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T10:56:20-07:00","id":1385624,"title":"","content":"I certainly don\u2019t disagree that neoliberal internationalism was often heavily cover for neoimperialism, and that neoimperialism is still very much there just more open. That has also always been a central pillar of the Union no matter how much they may want to pretend otherwise. This in many ways would correspond with my fourth proposed take on the current shift - that the Union\u2019s version of globalism, one built on authoritarian corporate colonialism, is inevitable from their view, so the current anti-internationalism backlash purely serves their interests in preventing the erection of democratic international institutions that could check that tide.<br /> <br /> I will note that we should keep in mind that in the context of MtA belief matters, even when from our POV it\u2019s a con. So the Union presumably still has an interest in promoting a Consensus that will accept global governance, even if the current neonationalism resurgence isn\u2019t really counter to that colonialist trend at all - it does weaken the paradigm they want to promote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-04-2020, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T11:20:37-07:00","id":1385627,"title":"","content":"I myself prefer to picture things in shades of gray. Or purple maybe. The Technocracy does bad things but hey have good reasons. The Traditions do good things, but their reasons are maybe not so good. I imagine that, in WWII, there were Mystics and Technocrats on both sides. I imagine the Order of Hermes being divided down the middle. As well as the NWO (or whatever they were called then).<br /> <br /> A different discussion on the subject of the Technocracy. The Convention names are dated and I hope they get revised alternate titles. I know that, for Trademark purposes, names and logos need to me maintained. What I would hope for is to provide alternate names as was done for a few traditions (Dreamspeakers/Kavadi) and so forth. NWO is so very 90's, and makes me think of wrestling and Hulk Hogan. Iteration X may have advanced a few steps. Iteration XIII? The name &quot;Syndicate&quot; is uninspiring and sounds like a mafia trope.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T11:43:41-07:00","id":1385629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1385624#post1385624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly don\u2019t disagree that neoliberal internationalism was often heavily cover for neoimperialism, and that neoimperialism is still very much there just more open. That has also always been a central pillar of the Union no matter how much they may want to pretend otherwise. This in many ways would correspond with my fourth proposed take on the current shift - that the Union\u2019s version of globalism, one built on authoritarian corporate colonialism, is inevitable from their view, so the current anti-internationalism backlash purely serves their interests in preventing the erection of democratic international institutions that could check that tide.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that your fourth proposed take on the current shift was most amenable to what I had suggested. I was merely trying to outline the specific value of that take above and beyond others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1385624#post1385624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will note that we should keep in mind that in the context of MtA belief matters, even when from our POV it\u2019s a con. So the Union presumably still has an interest in promoting a Consensus that will accept global governance, even if the current neonationalism resurgence isn\u2019t really counter to that colonialist trend at all - it does weaken the paradigm they want to promote.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for returning this discussion to this important point. I think something that I tried reflecting on in my original post was what does the Technocracy believe in, what do the Conventions believe in, what do they want the consensus to believe in, and how are they expected to show that belief? Moreover, I hope this new book elucidates the supremacy of Conventions over others in certain realms (e.g., the Syndicate taking more control in directing global governance through international corporate capitalism) and how their paradigms are more explicitly incommensurable (and in turn may weaken the paradigms of their colleagues). The introduction of terranorming provides an interesting avenue for explaining how a single Convention might implement possibly dissonant paradigms to achieve there goals. This is all to say I am left wondering if the belief in the Technocracy's ideals is more important for them or for the Consensus. Does the Technocracy need the Consensus to believe in the platonic ideal of a thing or just go along with the material relations of it? If their goal of global governance is based upon systems of control <b>and </b>dispossession, does it require that some people believe in one and be subject to the other? Can some Conventions be blind--in all their power--to the barriers to achieving their goals because of their implacable faith in their paradigms?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T12:47:57-07:00","id":1385639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1385627#post1385627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I myself prefer to picture things in shades of gray. Or purple maybe. The Technocracy does bad things but hey have good reasons. The Traditions do good things, but their reasons are maybe not so good. I imagine that, in WWII, there were Mystics and Technocrats on both sides. I imagine the Order of Hermes being divided down the middle. As well as the NWO (or whatever they were called then).<br /> <br /> A different discussion on the subject of the Technocracy. The Convention names are dated and I hope they get revised alternate titles. I know that, for Trademark purposes, names and logos need to me maintained. What I would hope for is to provide alternate names as was done for a few traditions (Dreamspeakers/Kavadi) and so forth. NWO is so very 90's, and makes me think of wrestling and Hulk Hogan. Iteration X may have advanced a few steps. Iteration XIII? The name &quot;Syndicate&quot; is uninspiring and sounds like a mafia trope.</div> </div> </div> </div>if I was going to rename the Syndicate, they\u2019d call themselves \u201cthe Invisible Hand.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T20:33:25-07:00","id":1385725,"title":"","content":"Driven as I am by my obsessions, I kicked in, as as of this posting the campaign is twenty bucks away from unlocking the Q Division bonus. It is my honest hope that the success for this project will convince the powers that be to keep the M20 train running past current projections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T20:34:59-07:00","id":1385726,"title":"","content":"And in the space of a breath it has tipped","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T21:59:18-07:00","id":1385743,"title":"","content":"I'll be surprised (pleasantly, but still surprised) if Paradox authorizes anything new for any of the X20 lines. <i>My</i> hope for the future of M20 after what's currently in the pipeline gets published is the Storyteller's Vault: as long as Paradox doesn't shut <i>that</i> down, none of the games it supports are truly dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T23:34:48-07:00","id":1385754,"title":"","content":"Mind you that Rich Bastard's Guide To Magick, and an M20 Victorian Mage Kickstarter are also coming. M20 ain't over just yet...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T23:49:19-07:00","id":1385756,"title":"","content":"Right. That's why I mentioned books still in the pipeline. <br /> <br /> And plans can change. If Paradox decides that \u201cOne World of Darkness\u201d isn't working out and chooses to let each of the WoD gamelines develop independently of each other, then it's entirely possible that we could end up with an M5 that existing Mage fans would willingly abandon M20 for \u2014 or that builds on what M20 has produced, keeping the M20 stuff relevant well into the life of M5. <br /> <br /> It's why I'm hoping that Onyx Path can get the rights to M5; I trust them to do it right, and won't worry about M20 coming to an end of they're the ones coming up with M20's successor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T00:38:12-07:00","id":1385765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1385400#post1385400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about making an edition that's designed to cater to the Storyteller's preference is that you don't get to dictate what that preference will be.<br /> <br /> With that said, the tone I've been getting from the manuscript so far has <i>not</i> been letting the Technocracy off the hook for anything. There has been acknowledgement after acknowledgement that the Union has done terrible things in the past and continues to do terrible things even today. So I have no concerns that the book will end up being tone-deaf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, it helps. But you're going to have a tone, like it or not; the consensus of MageAsc's reality may be malleable, but the gameline itself is only so much. You can't have the Union both do and <i>not</i> do a terrible thing, and <i>by definition</i> it has done terrible things if it's supposed to have brought about the current state of the world. (You can say the Union doesn't have the level of control it pretends to, but even that only goes so far as a mitigation device; push that too far, and you have a bunch of lucky idiots, not an interesting group of technological Awakened.)<br /> <br /> I can't say that I needed the Technocracy to ever play a science-focused Mage, even outside the two explicitly technological traditions. The thing to remember is the Technocracy <i>isn't actually about technology</i>, they're about <i>control</i>. They're the army claiming to bring freedom while pillaging resources; the empire that declares peace by killing all that oppose them.<br /> <br /> Or, at least, this has been their consistent portrayal up until now. Individuals under the Union's sway might care about science and technology very much, but the Union itself is mostly about making sure they stay in charge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:12:31-07:00","id":1385818,"title":"","content":"Well...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The second chapter manuscript that just dropped to Backers includes a small introduction story that is pretty much about them leveling a whole city block (including civilians) because of an out of control alien infestation that becomes uncontainable, and them covering it up. I think we're in good hands.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, that whole chapter is amaaazingly good. Union protocols and assets.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-05-2020, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T10:01:47-07:00","id":1385856,"title":"","content":"Ok, I have to say it, I'm laughing my ass reading the new chapter. Seriously, if it wasn't for backers only I would post here some of the expressions because they are fucking hilarious. I'm loving the whole &quot;I'm too tired of fucking bureaucrats, incompetent managers, and overconfident rookies&quot; tone of the narrator. XDXDXD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 05-05-2020, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T17:58:55-07:00","id":1385985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1385818#post1385818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The second chapter manuscript that just dropped to Backers includes a small introduction story that is pretty much about them leveling a whole city block (including civilians) because of an out of control alien infestation that becomes uncontainable, and them covering it up. I think we're in good hands.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, that whole chapter is amaaazingly good. Union protocols and assets.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>That helps. I look forward to the room to <i>play</i> someone under the Technocracy, but I didn't want it to just go all out into &quot;No srsly they're the good guys&quot;. That there's a trend in the fanbase to romanticize - and one I admit I fell prey to, for a little while - is because most of us <i>like</i> science and that was rather ill-served in Mage, I think. This is also in contrast to the Order of Reason one can play in historical Mage; <i>before</i> they had control and the majority of members were genuine in their beliefs.<br /> <br /> I need to catch up on the previews myself, actually.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T23:50:30-07:00","id":1386017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1385985#post1385985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That helps. I look forward to the room to <i>play</i> someone under the Technocracy, but I didn't want it to just go all out into &amp;quot;No srsly they're the good guys&amp;quot;. That there's a trend in the fanbase to romanticize - and one I admit I fell prey to, for a little while - is because most of us <i>like</i> science and that was rather ill-served in Mage, I think. This is also in contrast to the Order of Reason one can play in historical Mage; <i>before</i> they had control and the majority of members were genuine in their beliefs.<br /> <br /> I need to catch up on the previews myself, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Romanticize is an appropriately ironic word given the 90s romanticism that created 1ed Technocracy. M20 is doing a decent job updating the organization into an &quot;antagonist first, potential protagonist second&quot; for our modern context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T07:08:38-07:00","id":1386057,"title":"","content":"Any good villain is going to think they're the hero. So, I don't mind a Technocracy book being written from the perspective of them thinking themselves the good guys. I want cracks in that, like there for the Traditions in the core book. However, I do expect a book for a playable faction to be written from the idea they think they're the heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T08:09:09-07:00","id":1386080,"title":"","content":"This may seem like a strange time to mention Saint Augustine. He once put forth the idea that there is no such thing as &quot;Evil&quot;. What is being perceived is a relative lack of &quot;Good&quot;, or a definition of Good that is different somehow. People rarely think of themselves as the &quot;Bad Guy&quot;. Rather, they see themself as making the best of the situation at hand, and/or with a goal others do not comprehend.On a related note, that is why fascism depends on an &quot;outsider&quot; to vilianize. People can commit attrocious acts in the name of what they think of as &quot;Good&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T22:03:50-07:00","id":1386253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>El Barto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1386017#post1386017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Romanticize is an appropriately ironic word given the 90s romanticism that created 1ed Technocracy. M20 is doing a decent job updating the organization into an &quot;antagonist first, potential protagonist second&quot; for our modern context.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the Union but I feel like they get a bit too much slack. They're an anti-democratic secret society that engages in information control and financial abuse as its primary techniques. I feel like making these guys the &quot;good guys&quot; is an uncomfortable idea in the 21st century.<br /> <br /> They should be the faction of ICE, Fox News, Koch Brothers, and the Military Industrial Complex.<br /> <br /> I feel like making the sinister Illuminati into a progressive Left-leaning bunch of Utopians feeds into Right Wing conspiracy theories more than the progressive kind that the WOD has always dealt in.<br /> <br /> I admit that I kind of prefer the Seers to the Union even as I also note that the Union makes a GREAT player group if you want a dark X-Files-esque conspiracy game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T22:25:12-07:00","id":1386261,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy's presentation is one of those things that I feel will be an eternal debate in Mage and one that is ultimately without conclusion because most arguments are at least partially correct and valid.<br /> <br /> Personally I do agree that the Technocratic Union is a dark organization and that many of its actions cannot be considered moral by any modern standard. However in the moral relativism of the World of Nightmares, one could argue it is the lesser of others evils. The Camarilla and Sabbat, the Garou Nation, The Union and Council, the Hierarchy, and Concordia. Each of these organizations has a reason to exist and each is horrific in its own way. <br /> <br /> Also take into consideration the phrase that is used to define the World of Darkness: 'Gothic-Punk'. Shadows fill the whole of the setting, from that we can see the gothic elements. Yet within those shadows, people fight. Fight to survive, to be free, to be moral, to be independent, to do good. The world is defined by both respects.<br /> <br /> Different times and different people will want to play different games. Some will want to delve into the psychology of what makes someone willing to be a Sabbat crusader or an NWO Black Suit wet-worker. Others will want to play rebels within or without the system, trying to ensure as best they can.<br /> <br /> Keeping that in mind, a range of scenarios and circumstances is built into the setting. Factions are built with potential to be played at both extremes. This means that for instance the Technocratic Union as a setting element fosters both cold-blooded authoritarian directives and eugenics while allowing for higher ideals and the potential for those inspired and resilient enough to fight to reach out and fight the system and do what they believe to be right, regardless of price.<br /> <br /> So for me, I can understand why people argue both sides. The Union by necessity is not any organization which the average person would want to exist. Yet in the context of the World of Darkness it has its place. The role it plays in any specific story depends on the needs of the chronicle.<br /> <br /> It can be a shadowy syndicate of conspiracy, a ruthless military juggernaut, an icy system for manipulation, or explorers into the Great beyond. Or something else or none of the above.<br /> <br /> It is always exactly what the circumstances require.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T22:25:48-07:00","id":1386262,"title":"","content":"The problem with swinging the pendulum over to black hat Union is that then we run into the problematic depiction of &quot;conventional science = neo-fascists.&quot; As a reminder, no the NWO and Syndicate are not the only conventions in the Union, and it's kinda weird to just pretend the other three conventions don't matter. <br /> <br /> And no, I don't think making the VAs or Etherites fill that label works either, since their whole thing is &quot;alternative science&quot;, which suggests that conventional science doesn't work.<br /> <br /> Taking a look over IRL...do you really think scientists like having their findings on climate change or renewable energy be dismissed by politicians? <br /> <br /> No, they're not the flawless, but conversely <i><b>the Technocrats are NOT Pentex</b></i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:22:20-07:00","id":1386275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1386253#post1386253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love the Union but I feel like they get a bit too much slack. They're an anti-democratic secret society that engages in information control and financial abuse as its primary techniques. I feel like making these guys the &quot;good guys&quot; is an uncomfortable idea in the 21st century.<br /> <br /> They should be the faction of ICE, Fox News, Koch Brothers, and the Military Industrial Complex.<br /> <br /> I feel like making the sinister Illuminati into a progressive Left-leaning bunch of Utopians feeds into Right Wing conspiracy theories more than the progressive kind that the WOD has always dealt in.<br /> <br /> I admit that I kind of prefer the Seers to the Union even as I also note that the Union makes a GREAT player group if you want a dark X-Files-esque conspiracy game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/527674-the-politics-of-m20\">a thread</a> that I think ought to be reviewed on occasion; and this may be one of those occasions. In particular, there's one part of the thread where it's mentioned that one of the successes of Mage has been that it <i>hasn't</i> tried to align the in-game factions with real-world politics: the fact that it <i>isn't</i> \u201cthe noble, progressive Traditions vs. the nutty right-wing Technocrats\u201d is a <i>feature</i>, not a flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:25:24-07:00","id":1386278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1386275#post1386275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/527674-the-politics-of-m20\">a thread</a> that I think ought to be reviewed on occasion; and this may be one of those occasions. In particular, there's one part of the thread where it's mentioned that one of the successes of Mage has been that it <i>hasn't</i> tried to align the in-game factions with real-world politics: the fact that it <i>isn't</i> \u201cthe noble, progressive Traditions vs. the nutty right-wing Technocrats\u201d is a <i>feature</i>, not a flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? I'm actually of the mind artwork including real life political commentary is a feature not a bug.<br /> <br /> See Werewolf.<br /> <br /> But to each their own.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:33:20-07:00","id":1386279,"title":"","content":"For me, I like that any of the factions can be looked at in several perspectives to create a vast number of potential analogues. <br /> <br /> The Council can have granola chewing lefties alongside blood and soil race supremacists. The Union can have fiscally conservative Syndicate members genuinely interested in economic stability, authoritarian leftist bulsheviks, or clear-sighted scientific juggernauts and crafty but idealistic political operators.<br /> <br /> Each side can have elements that are light, dark, and grey. Multi-faceted natures and presentations for both give near countless opportunities for utilization of every faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:50:18-07:00","id":1386288,"title":"","content":"Yes; that's what I was trying to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:57:33-07:00","id":1386293,"title":"","content":"That certainly provides a multitude of options but does it work for an organization as ruthless and monolithic as the Union? I will say I always did like the idea the NWO was at each other's throats during the Cold War as implied by RAGE ACROSS RUSSIA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T00:17:51-07:00","id":1386297,"title":"","content":"I pretty much am on the side that says that all factions (sans Nephandi) being pretty much shades of gray - including the Union - is a big feature of Mage, yes.<br /> Some might be considered a darker gray than others, of course. I mean, the Traditions certainly seem to be in general, to put it simply, a more humane and friendler organization than the Union.<br /> <br /> But. Here is the big but when it comes to Mage: That's pure, current circumstance of the modern times and the power balance.<br /> <br /> During the olde times of dragons and castles, supposedly certain groups of wizards and willworkers were so bad, that a group of enlightened people decided &quot;We have to stop this madness. We have to organize and pull humanity out of the darkness and fear and empower it from those insane, cruel bastards.&quot;. It's the very origin of the Order Of Reason, and they were damn good guys at the start - and on the contrary, the 'wizards' they were looking at (which were certainly not *all* willworkers of all cultures, but focused on Europe) were aloof, distant from the common folk and doing horrible things at times.<br /> <br /> One of the core themes of Mage is that power can corrupt, and for the longest time (i.e. 1st to Revised with a slowly declining curve) the Union had that absolute power, with the Traditions struggling. The more that 'absolute power' of the Union waned, the more their darkest of greys (Which was a pure black at the start of 1st ed, really) started to lighten a bit, the Union's good elements came to the fore, and a bit more of the Tradition's problems became apparent.<br /> <br /> Now in M20, post-avatar-storm and with the Nephandi gaining ground, the Union losing its grip and the Traditions (and Disparates) not being absolutely backed into a corner anymore...yeah, it makes sense that it all becomes quite a mixed set of morals, problems and shades of grey again, because in the factions both the types of people that strive for control and power, as well as those with high ideals and good hearts become more active and apparent in the struggle.<br /> <br /> The difference between the Union and the rest is, right now, that we have clearly documented results of them having too much power in the last hundreds of years. The Traditions can claim 'we're the good guys, we've always been the underdogs', but what'd happen if the Trads had lots of power for hundreds of years is up for a lot of debate and what-ifs - but in the end, human nature has its ways of ruining good things and the best of intentions.<br /> <br /> In the end, 1st ed aside, the Nephandi are the only group that honestly believe and know that they are the Bad Guys with a capital E in Evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-07-2020, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T11:02:10-07:00","id":1386434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1386293#post1386293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That certainly provides a multitude of options but does it work for an organization as ruthless and monolithic as the Union? I will say I always did like the idea the NWO was at each other's throats during the Cold War as implied by RAGE ACROSS RUSSIA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...I'd take anything on what one splat is said in the book belonging to a different splat with a grain of salt, honestly.<br /> <br /> But otherwise, like I said: the Union is not Pentex. I can't exactly dictate what happens at other people's tables, obviously, but if you start twisting the Union into Pentex then...why not actually use Pentex?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T12:30:36-07:00","id":1386451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1386434#post1386434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well...I'd take anything on what one splat is said in the book belonging to a different splat with a grain of salt, honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't think Soviet NWO and American NWO had any issues?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But otherwise, like I said: the Union is not Pentex. I can't exactly dictate what happens at other people's tables, obviously, but if you start twisting the Union into Pentex then...why not actually use Pentex? </div> </div> </div>I'd say the Templars from Assassins Creed is a better organization to compare my conception of the Union to rather than Pentex. Pentex is a bunch of Nephandi controlling an enormous demon cult. The Technocracy as I think a dark version would be of would be an organization that believes in controlling Sleepers for their own good and keeping the leash around them tightly because they can't be trusted. They are the people who want to have a magocracy for all eternity.<br /> <br /> The Traditions want to remove the veil of secrecy from the eyes of humanity and show them the truth.<br /> <br /> It's not the way they're presented in the game since 1st Edition but I always liked the &quot;Stasis&quot; vs &quot;Dynamic&quot; conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T15:06:50-07:00","id":1386507,"title":"","content":"Willworkers are proud people so the idea that factions would appear that have contradictory ideologies, such as Cold War NWO factions, makes perfect sense to me. I can see why one would also say they are largely restrained in their tensions via Control yet conversely sometimes it's in everyone's best interests for the factions to duke it out or bringing them to heel would cost more then it would gain.<br /> <br /> The notion of a Technocratic Civil War has been brewing for a long time so I can certainly see why a Storyteller might be interested in invoking that and playing upon prior tensions, even those smoothed down as best they could be. <br /> <br /> Plus aye, the Stasis vs. Dynamic conflict is certainly rife with opportunity and can be well used with the Union vs. Council particularly. I could also see it used as an interesting way to plot Mage growth as they develop and simultaneously become more and more invested in their position, both politically and philosophically, all the while becoming slowly less reliant upon said tools to actually work their Will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T15:22:13-07:00","id":1386792,"title":"","content":"New Stretch Goal is up. At $143k, the Unlikely Allies chapter in the Companion will include details to cross-faction play between the Technocrats and...Orphans.<br /> <br /> Man, did the T:R devs also think it was weird the Orphans were lumped in with the Disparates? lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T15:49:26-07:00","id":1386801,"title":"","content":"Eh. What would you cut to make room for another page to present Orphans on the same level as the Traditions, Technocracy, and Disparates? And what would you put on that page that isn't already adequately handled on the existing two-page Orphans write-up? <br /> <br /> They had to put the Orphans <i>somewhere</i>, and the Disparates were the least bad choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-08-2020, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T21:05:09-07:00","id":1386897,"title":"","content":"Isn't the point of being an Orphan being that you don't belong to any organized group? I mean, there's already an organization of Orphans in the Hollow Ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T21:12:56-07:00","id":1386898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1386897#post1386897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the point of being an Orphan being that you don't belong to any organized group? I mean, there's already an organization of Orphans in the Hollow Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and that's why.<br /> <br /> Just that it was weird to lump then in with the Disparates, when their whole thing was that they were mages that didn't align themselves with any of the major factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T21:31:19-07:00","id":1386901,"title":"","content":"That's why I described it as the \u201cleast bad option\u201d rather than \u201cthe best option\u201d. It <i>does</i> kind of fit, in that the Disparates are essentially \u201cthe guys who aren't Traditionists or Technocrats\u201d. Yeah, there's the bit about the beginnings of Disparate Alliance; but that's one of those things that optional in M20: it's entirely possible that the various Crafts described in that part of M20 are in fact well and truly Disparate, with each Craft operating solely on its own. In that context, the Orphans aren't that bad of a fit.<br /> <br /> And like I said, they had to go <i>somewhere</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T06:23:19-07:00","id":1386965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1386901#post1386901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And like I said, they had to go <i>somewhere</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it wouldn't have been too hard after the DA chapter to make a &quot;Those that doesn't fit&quot; page with the Orphan double page there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T00:43:58-07:00","id":1388261,"title":"","content":"Having read through the collection so far, I do appreciate the way that the Technocracy is being portrayed. It really is 