:[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T12:46:04-07:00","id":1391238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1390708#post1390708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HAH. VINDICATION!! Because it makes <i>absolutely no goddamn sense</i> that the Union would stand by and just let climate change happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a darker Union, tragedies and disasters are not problems but opportunities. Here's how the Technocracy might handle a situation a bit too similar to our present one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/qJegc9eEG8M\" data-code=\"qJegc9eEG8M\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/qJegc9eEG8M/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T13:19:03-07:00","id":1391243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391238#post1391238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a darker Union, tragedies and disasters are not problems but opportunities. Here's how the Technocracy might handle a situation a bit too similar to our present one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/qJegc9eEG8M\" data-code=\"qJegc9eEG8M\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/qJegc9eEG8M/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I differ from the video in the implications it's making about just <i>who</i> it is that sees the various tragedies and disasters as opportunities rather than problems; but I can very easily see the Technocratic Union being aligned with those who do. <br /> <br /> And in-game, I think that the current pandemic, and the Union's response to it, could be the catalyst for Navalon breaking from the Union. And then pursuing a Solarpunk future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T14:11:41-07:00","id":1391258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391238#post1391238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a darker Union, tragedies and disasters are not problems but opportunities.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would still make no sense because the NWO do not represent the totality of the Union's activities.<br /> <br /> If they were that flippant on not trying to fix climate change, then conventions like the Progenitors, particular Syndicate members, and earthside Void Engineers would have no reason not to leave the Union in large numbers.<br /> <br /> And in general lead to problematic implications of &quot;scientists are complicit in allowing climate change to happen&quot; which is factually not true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T14:49:23-07:00","id":1391267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391258#post1391258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would still make no sense because the NWO do not represent the totality of the Union's activities.<br /> <br /> If they were that flippant on not trying to fix climate change, then conventions like the Progenitors, particular Syndicate members, and earthside Void Engineers would have no reason not to leave the Union in large numbers.<br /> <br /> And in general lead to problematic implications of &quot;scientists are complicit in allowing climate change to happen&quot; which is factually not true.</div> </div> </div> </div>That assumes the NWO is the dark heart of the Union rather than the entirety of it.<br /> <br /> But I see the issue.<br /> <br /> I don't see Unionists as scientists. I see them as a secret conspiracy bent on world conquest. They just employ scientists. Their appeal is not YAY SCIENCE (or at least only YAY SCIENCE) it is, &quot;We can't do worse than your present leaders.&quot; Which is a fair argument, I think.<br /> <br /> They're the Mister House ending of Fallout: New Vegas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:03:10-07:00","id":1391271,"title":"","content":"A darker Union isn't representative of scientists; it's representative of technocrats:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Technocracy: the government or control of society or industry by an elite of technical experts.</div><br /> The argument isn't that the Technocracy would deliberately inflict suffering on people \u2014 although with the Technephandi metaplot, just might \u2014 it's that they're likely to be more interested in \u201cnot letting a crisis go to waste\u201d: there are things you can do during a crisis that you wouldn't be able to do otherwise. Despite the video that CTPhipps linked to (which leads heavily into the Fallen Technocracy), I don't think that the Union would be doing nothing to stop climate change, the pandemic, or whatever other crisis you wish to bring up; it's that, at the very least, they're likely to Be multitasking, with one of those tasks being to find solutions to the crisis while another being to use the opportunities that the crisis presents to extend their influence. <br /> <br /> And it's disturbingly easy for a technocrat to develop tunnel vision; moreso even than their desire to be in charge, that's probably their single biggest flaw. In this regard, those who see crises as opportunities to push their agendas often lose track of the fact that resolving the crisis is itself a goal: \u201cwe've accomplished so much since this started; just think of how much more we could accomplish if this were to go on just a <i>little bit</i> longer\u2026\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:15:47-07:00","id":1391279,"title":"","content":"I do not view the Technocracy as scientists. They are wizards who are lying to themselves and pretending to be scientists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:23:49-07:00","id":1391286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391267#post1391267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see Unionists as scientists. I see them as a secret conspiracy bent on world conquest. They just employ scientists. Their appeal is not YAY SCIENCE (or at least only YAY SCIENCE) it is, &quot;We can't do worse than your present leaders.&quot; Which is a fair argument, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't <i>quite</i> agree with this. I think the Union <i>is</i> composed of scientists; but they're scientists who have fallen into a trap where they've placed a bit <i>too</i> much faith in their science: they tend to represent what's bad about \u201cTechnology Holds All the Answers\u201d as well as what's good about it.<br /> <br /> Both \u201cthey're not really scientists\u201d and \u201cthey're merely control freaks\u201d are overly simplistic takes on the Technocracy, as I see it. (By the way, credit for my preferred view of the Technocracy goes to Malcolm Sheppard, who did a far better job explaining this about two or three forums ago.) One of the reasons I push for <i>not</i> presenting the Technocrats as deluded wizards is that that gets in the way of a far more interesting take on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-24-2020, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T16:47:08-07:00","id":1391338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391286#post1391286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't <i>quite</i> agree with this. I think the Union <i>is</i> composed of scientists; but they're scientists who have fallen into a trap where they've placed a bit <i>too</i> much faith in their science: they tend to represent what's bad about \u201cTechnology Holds All the Answers\u201d as well as what's good about it.<br /> <br /> Both \u201cthey're not really scientists\u201d and \u201cthey're merely control freaks\u201d are overly simplistic takes on the Technocracy, as I see it. (By the way, credit for my preferred view of the Technocracy goes to Malcolm Sheppard, who did a far better job explaining this about two or three forums ago.) One of the reasons I push for <i>not</i> presenting the Technocrats as deluded wizards is that that gets in the way of a far more interesting take on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit iffier and think it really depends on your Paradigm (*rimshot*) and what the themes of the campaign are. Which is a very mage thing when you think about it. The question of what the Technocracy is depends, I think, on what the chronicle is about. Which is something that the M20 supplement handles well.<br /> <br /> 1. Going with the &quot;deluded wizards&quot; version, I actually had a very solid chronicle with a friend where the theme of the campaign was the pointlessness of the Ascension War. The conflict was between the Technocracy [explitcly wizards who knew how to do magic] wanting to uphold the Masquerade-equivalent and work coincidental magic through science.<br /> <br /> They knew exactly what they were doing and were trying to exterminate the Traditions because they felt that if you screwed with a Sleeper's brain too much, it would collapse. The Traditions were fighting brutally against the Union because they all wanted to do their own kind of coincidental magic and hated that the Union was the dominant paradigm. The campaign emphasized the sheer selfishness and wastefulness of the conflict that they were all fighting over what, magically, the equivalent of &quot;Mac or PC&quot;?<br /> <br /> It was very much a Revised take on the subject (before Revised) because the answer was that the Union and Traditions should have been teaming up to help humanity or at least fighting off the real threats.<br /> <br /> 2. Conversely, you could also do the &quot;Technocrats have no understanding of magic&quot; which is an extreme in the opposite direction. The idea that Unionists really have no idea what Traditionalists are doing and all their theories are grossly incorrect. They see themselves as basically inside a Call of Cthulhu game where a bunch of people are using science like the Ghostbusters and Doc Savage against horrifying alien weirdness. This could be used to emphasize that their obsessive devotion to their paradigm has actually made them ignorant of the true nature of reality.<br /> <br /> 3. Then there's Seers of Thrones-lite where the Technocracy isn't scientiffic at all because they CREATE the laws of reality. They define what the laws of physics are as accepted by the Masses, medical discoveries, and progress of technology is according to the Time Table. Whole rules of the universe may be enforced by their control and they aren't so much all-powerful as still wielding control beyond what most mortals could imagine. You can't be a scientist in such an organization because there's nothing to discover. If you want there to be a new planet, you submit a form, don't build a telescope.<br /> <br /> All of them are equally valid takes, IMHO, but they create dramatically different settings. I've always felt this is one of those things that overlaps with the Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts. A lot of people have just as different views on them as the Union depending on how you think science functions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T16:50:20-07:00","id":1391340,"title":"","content":"Dataweaver:<br /> I see your point. But the *are* wizards. It may be a fault in my imagination, but I find it impossible to see them as not wizards. The feats they perform are not possible with the science of our reality. It is a fictional world, I do understand that. But whatever they want to call it, they are still working magick (with a &quot;k&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T17:02:02-07:00","id":1391351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391340#post1391340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dataweaver:<br /> I see your point. But the *are* wizards. It may be a fault in my imagination, but I find it impossible to see them as not wizards. The feats they perform are not possible with the science of our reality. It is a fictional world, I do understand that. But whatever they want to call it, they are still working magick (with a &quot;k&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly, T20 actually feels a lot like the Sons of Ether as I've always run them.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, what we're doing functions like magic but we're treating it through the lens of scientists studying its rules and properties.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then again, I've never run the Sons of Ether as WACKY. They've always been serious scientists with a very difficult problem of trying to measure the turtles all the way down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T18:53:16-07:00","id":1391380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391340#post1391340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dataweaver:<br /> I see your point. But the *are* wizards. It may be a fault in my imagination, but I find it impossible to see them as not wizards. The feats they perform are not possible with the science of our reality. It is a fictional world, I do understand that. But whatever they want to call it, they are still working magick (with a &quot;k&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391351#post1391351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weirdly, T20 actually feels a lot like the Sons of Ether as I've always run them.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, what we're doing functions like magic but we're treating it through the lens of scientists studying its rules and properties.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then again, I've never run the Sons of Ether as WACKY. They've always been serious scientists with a very difficult problem of trying to measure the turtles all the way down.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's it in a nutshell. That said, my personal take on it tweaks things slightly so that there actually is some justification for their claim that they're not doing the same thing that mages do. And while the changes that I make do change the letter of what the game claims to be true, I will argue strenuously that they keep the spirit of the game.<br /> <br /> Brucato just released an STV supplement called <b>Mage Made Easy</b>. I'm still reading through it, but what I've gathered thus far is that it's essentially his advice on what he thinks Mage should be like. There is a point that he makes early on in the book to the effect that the point of the game is people who can change the world. Everything else is second to that. Even \u201cthrough Enlightened Will\u201d (with the emphasis on Will) is secondary to that. To my mind, the divide between the Technocracy and the Superstitionists is that the latter tend to put the focus on the will, while the technocracy puts the focus on the enlightenment. <br /> <br /> Put another way, a Mystic changes the world through force of will, with his belief, practices, and instruments focusing that will. Thus the term \u201cWillworking\u201d. But to a technomancer, the key ingredient is enlightenment \u2014 a gut-level understanding of what the <i>real</i> rules are and what can be done with them. <br /> <br /> In my head-canon, this distinction between Willworking vs. Enlightened Science is what's behind the rules divide between mystics and technomancers, both in terms of the different schedules for discarding instruments and also in terms of the personal investment that most mages need in order to make Talismans vs. the Union's ability to make them without that personal investment. They both do things that change the world; but they do so in two different ways that have practical differences, with each being capable of something the other isn't capable of (Working Without Focus and discarding instruments in the case of Willworking, and making Devices without personal investments in the case of Enlightened Science). <br /> <br /> So no, technocrats are not delusional wizards. They're very close cousins, but they're something slightly different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-24-2020, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T19:06:05-07:00","id":1391386,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think that its a central part of the game that Technocrats and Traditionalists are fighting over nothing. Enlightenment versus Awakening is the &quot;Civil War over transubstantiation&quot; that Gulivers Travels made fun of by comparing it to which way to butter bread.<br /> <br /> &quot;We both want Mass Ascension but their way is WRONG.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T19:44:25-07:00","id":1391402,"title":"","content":"\u2026and this gets back to something we were discussing earlier: I don't think they <i>do</i> both want Mass Ascension. I think the Technocracy wants an overall improvement of the human condition, to Utopian levels even; but I don't think they'd consider that to be a Mass Ascension, as Mass Ascension is predicated on Mass Awakening, which the Union views as a nightmare scenario: the last thing the Technocracy wants is for every monster, madman, and fool to have the power to change the world. And they have a point; I'm sure that <i>everyone</i> can name someone in a position of power who they wish hadn't received that power. <br /> <br /> I think that there are fundamental differences between the Technocracy and the Traditions, and that those differences matter. It's just not as clear-cut as \u201cTraditions good, Technocracy bad\u201d, or even \u201cTraditions right, Technocracy wrong\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T17:44:40-07:00","id":1391572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391267#post1391267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see Unionists as scientists.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391279#post1391279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not view the Technocracy as scientists. They are wizards who are lying to themselves and pretending to be scientists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still disagree, mostly for the same reasons given by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> <br /> <br /> But even then, among the splats the Union is still depicted as holding conventional scientists among their ranks, to an extent that none of the Traditions or Crafts hold. Etherites are generally portrayed as &quot;alternative/fringe scientists&quot; who engage in practices and theories considered unorthodox by the wider scientific community. While some of the other groups you COULD stretch them to be proper scientists...but we're getting into the grey territory of edge cases, so let's not.<br /> <br /> And even then...the mechanics don't really reflect &quot;deluded wizards&quot; considering how Technocrats cannot, under any circumstances, drop Instruments when raising Genius...and that they can only do that if they leave the Union.<br /> <br /> (Granted, I'll give that this is a larger issue on how much Paradigm should/shouldn't be hard-coded into mechanics, including the debate regarding the Technocrat Spheres even being a Thing or not)<br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Anyways, we achieved both novella stretch goals.<br /> <br /> Next up at $171k, we get the Truth Beyond Paradox PDF being added to the rewards list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T17:51:26-07:00","id":1391573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391572#post1391572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Still disagree, mostly for the same reasons given by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a><br /> <br /> But even then, among the splats the Union is still depicted as holding conventional scientists among their ranks, to an extent that none of the Traditions or Crafts hold. Etherites are generally portrayed as &quot;alternative/fringe scientists&quot; who engage in practices and theories considered unorthodox by the wider scientific community. While some of the other groups you COULD stretch them to be proper scientists...but we're getting into the grey territory of edge cases, so let's not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, the thing is that can you say that Etherites are fringe scientists when their experimentation is with testable proven results? Etherites also have a magazine that peer reviews them.<br /> <br /> It's just Etherites are studying magic so that it looks alternative and weird. I don't think we've ever seen Etherites do homeopathy or magnets. They still have Science and Technology scores. It's just with magic that they can bend (but not break) physics around them.<br /> <br /> Or to use a common media example:<br /> <br /> &quot;Doc Brown is considered a crackpot because he believes in time travel. Doc Brown has also constructed a functioning time machine.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T18:23:43-07:00","id":1391578,"title":"","content":"The key difference between Ether Science and the Enlightened Science practiced by the Technocracy is that the former rejects reductionism while the latter embraces it. <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Reductionism:</b> the practice of analyzing and describing a complex phenomenon in terms of phenomena that are held to represent a simpler or more fundamental level, especially when this is said to provide a sufficient explanation.</div>In the Technocracy, this manifests as the belief that there is one best way to do things, and that the alternatives are inferior, dangerous, or both. At their worst, the Technocracy has taken to trying to \u201csimplify\u201d reality to conform to their models of how it <i>should</i> be. This includes increasingly isolating the Umbra from Conventional Space so that the latter can be explored and exploited without the danger of interference from the Umbrood; but it also involves attempting to modify humanity so that it's more predictable and subject to their elegant models of human behavior. That's something that would be insanely stupid in our world; but when you <i>can</i> literally change the world, it's actually a viable (if morally questionable) strategy. <br /> <br /> By contrast, the Etherites are anti-reductionist: they can and do explore multiple ways of doing things; and their strategy for Mass Ascension is to expand the scope of things that the Consensus will accept until the Consensus will accept anything, rendering all Ether Science (what their comrades call \u201cMagick\u201d) Coincidental. The Union also wants to expand what the Masses can do on their own. But at best, they see the Etherite approach as being overcomplicated; and at worst, they see it as actively detrimental, risking a paralysis of the Masses due to an overwhelming excess of options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-30-2020, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T05:30:09-07:00","id":1391670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391402#post1391402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and this gets back to something we were discussing earlier: I don't think they <i>do</i> both want Mass Ascension. I think the Technocracy wants an overall improvement of the human condition, to Utopian levels even</div> </div> </div> </div>Syndicate revised spelled this out in the first chapter, with the cadence of seasoned salesman even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T07:17:50-07:00","id":1391675,"title":"","content":"\u2026and Unit 8 did <i>not</i> live up to my expectations at all. Nothing about possible Future Fates for the Union, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T08:18:44-07:00","id":1391681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391675#post1391675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and Unit 8 did <i>not</i> live up to my expectations at all. Nothing about possible Future Fates for the Union, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Same here, I feel scammed. Not a word on the possible Reorg that was promised in Unit 1. Everything here is what we got from revised convention books. The only new things are a paragraph on a possible alliance with the Traditions without any further details and that Control may not be fallen but marauder.<br /> <br /> I mean, really, that's deeply insulting to the backers.<br /> <br /> I have the impression that this whole Unit 7 and 8 was rushed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T08:49:19-07:00","id":1391686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391675#post1391675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and Unit 8 did <i>not</i> live up to my expectations at all. Nothing about possible Future Fates for the Union, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you, Unit 7 and 8, especially 8, feel like and afterthought and I have voiced my disappointment in the kickstarter comments. I sincerely hope that they correct this in the final version. It has been an excellent book so far, it would be a pity to have such a lackluster sections in an otherwise excellent book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T08:58:44-07:00","id":1391689,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say scammed, but I do wish Unit 8 was bigger. I think it's the shortest Unit. What's there is good, I just want more of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T09:07:07-07:00","id":1391690,"title":"","content":"Something I'd like to see would be for the Threat Marauder section to be heavily revised, possibly even completely rewritten. Instead, I want to see something about the Union in Denial:<br /> <br /> One problem with pushing the notion that there's one best way to do things is that it's remarkably easy to come to the conclusion that alternatives aren't just inferior, but fundamentally flawed. This can eventually lead the Scientist into the trap of Denial, where he starts to actively not believe in Magick. Mind you, this is <i>not</i> true of the typical Technocratic operative; but it <i>is</i> a problem in the Union, in that an unusually high percentage of Technocratic Quiets are this kind of Denial. Examples from earlier editions where Technocrats spoke as if Science was real and Magick was fake would be retconned here as examples of agents in Denial. <br /> <br /> And this form of Denial is particularly prone towards generating Negation Men, a variety of Marauders (in Denial instead of Madness) who instinctively trigger Countermagick against Effects that they don't believe in and who count as Witnesses against it, despite being Enlightened. Instead of Threat Marauder, I'd have \u201cThreat Negation\u201d \u2014 and I'd have the NWO and the Progenitors on the forefront of identifying and combatting it, much like the Void Engineers are on the forefront of battling Threat Null. (NWO because of their emphasis on psychology, and Progenitors as the psychiatric arm of the fight.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T10:36:48-07:00","id":1391713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391689#post1391689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say scammed, but I do wish Unit 8 was bigger. I think it's the shortest Unit. What's there is good, I just want more of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we are promised that this Unit would contain &quot;deep dive into metaplot possibilities&quot; some of them being described as of &quot;earth shattering implications for the world of darkness&quot;<br /> <br /> None of that is given. The entire part about reorganisation of the union was postponed into unit 8 and it doesn't appear at all.<br /> <br /> So I think scammed is the right term as we didn't obtained what was promised","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T10:43:32-07:00","id":1391715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391713#post1391713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well we are promised that this Unit would contain &quot;deep dive into metaplot possibilities&quot; some of them being described as of &quot;earth shattering implications for the world of darkness&quot;<br /> <br /> None of that is given. The entire part about reorganisation of the union was postponed into unit 8 and it doesn't appear at all.<br /> <br /> So I think scammed is the right term as we didn't obtained what was promised</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A draft manuscript you pledged towards but haven't even paid for is not a promise. I 100% agree Unit 8 does not address the reorg at all and does not contain a deep dive into any metaplot other than Threat Null. However, Onyx Path has a good track record of listening to feedback like this and making adjustments. So, you can decide if you want to continue to pledge or not based on what you've read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T10:48:13-07:00","id":1391719,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I wouldn't dream of pulling out. But I really, really, <i>really</i> want them to revise and expand Unit 8. It's weak sauce as written, and doesn't live up to its own hype:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Unit 8:The Parallax View</b> takes a deep dive into metaplot options, discussing every significant Future Fate that affects the Technocratic Union. Options are provided for incorporating, ignoring, or subverting these metaplot options, and entire new metaplot options are introduced. The tools in this chapter permit the Storyteller and players to shape the Union to their own vision, giving you everything you need to carry your Technocracy Reloaded game into the past, present, or future.</div>That's what we were told would be in Unit 8; but it isn't what actually made it into Unit 8.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-26-2020, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T10:58:54-07:00","id":1391722,"title":"","content":"I also am not going to back out, but I've put my 2 cents in the kickstarter comments about wanting a beefier Unit 8. I just thought &quot;scamming&quot; was an overly-loaded term to be using for something we've been reading for free (at least for the next 47 hours or so.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T11:39:22-07:00","id":1391732,"title":"","content":"Although at this stage, wouldn't surprise me if Paradox tightened their grip on the writer's hands declaring: &quot;Woah woah, hold on a sec, don't write anything that could contradict M5!!!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T11:41:52-07:00","id":1391734,"title":"","content":"Frankly, most of my suggestions for Unit 8 are things that I'd like to see in M5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T00:15:32-07:00","id":1391875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391732#post1391732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although at this stage, wouldn't surprise me if Paradox tightened their grip on the writer's hands declaring: &amp;quot;Woah woah, hold on a sec, don't write anything that could contradict M5!!!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't be the first time they've done that to M20, though they didn't futz with Book of the Fallen as far as I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T05:13:03-07:00","id":1391898,"title":"","content":"I admit to wanting more about &quot;The Union collapses&quot;, &quot;Nephandi take over and the non-corrupted Unionists have to join the Traditions&quot;, and so on.<br /> <br /> However, the rest of the book is amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T08:00:38-07:00","id":1391940,"title":"","content":"Anyways, 4th novella has been achieved, so looks like we're getting a Union anthology out of the whole thing.<br /> <br /> So at $185k, we have the addition of an at-cost PoD coupon for the T:R Companion, $190k for a similar PoD coupon for M20 core, and at $195k a pay bonus for the whole creative team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T22:13:19-07:00","id":1392121,"title":"","content":"Sadly, I'm barely interested in game-related fiction, so reaching &quot;We'll publish more fiction&quot; stretch goal usually leaves me cold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T22:30:35-07:00","id":1392124,"title":"","content":"Likewise. That said, I've already pledged; and I'm already going to get my money's worth out of the Kickstarter. Unless and until they include \u201cadd-on\u201d Stretch Goals for things that I'm interested in, I'm not their target audience anymore. (If I was in a situation where physical books were a viable option for me, these latest stretch goals would have been golden. Unfortunately, I don't have the space for a physical library.) If there are those who love game-related fiction and who have been sitting on the sidelines, the novella stretch goals are a good thing to offer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T08:04:12-07:00","id":1392193,"title":"","content":"And now we got the PoD coupon for the Companion and the M20 core add-on. <br /> <br /> No clue if we'll make it the $5k sprint for the pay bonus...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T11:14:44-07:00","id":1392265,"title":"","content":"It's funded. $193,630 and 2365 backers.<br /> <br /> And on a personal note, this Kickstarter gave me a birthday present (my birthday is Saturday). Five years ago (I think) when the M20 Kickstarter took place, I couldn't justify the funds for a Deluxe Hardcover and had to settle for the standard hardcover. This morning, one of the Deluxe Archivist slots opened up, and I grabbed it. So I'm finally going to get what I wanted to get way back when M20 launched. Happy (early) birthday to me! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-28-2020, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T23:38:42-07:00","id":1394730,"title":"","content":"Crap -- Missed pledging for this. How do I use backerkit to get a copy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T06:04:50-07:00","id":1398761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1385388#post1385388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Add me to the &quot;concerned that the response to 'people want to play the evil, literally-backed-the-Nazis group as heroes'</div> </div> </div> </div>So you have concerns about people playing or wanting to play ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Japan, the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Akashic_Brotherhood\" target=\"_blank\">Akashic Brotherhood</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dreamspeakers_(MTAs)\" target=\"_blank\">Dreamspeakers</a> devoted to Shintoism served the empires as spies and assassins </div> </div> </div>Akashics and Dreamspeakers?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Europe, the Iron Circle of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Verbena\" target=\"_blank\">Verbena</a>, preserver of the secrets of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Valdaermen\" target=\"_blank\">Valdaermen</a>, inserted themselves into the occult societies of the Nazis and began a hunt against rival Awakened, even from among their allies in the Traditions.<sup><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_War_II_(WOD)#cite_note-TBV28-15\" target=\"_blank\">[16]</a></sup> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Order_of_Hermes\" target=\"_blank\">Hermetics</a> were part of numerous occult societies and threw their weight behind the Party. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Order of Hermes largely supported the Axis powers, seeing the influence of occultism in the higher ranks of Nazi Germany as a good sign </div> </div> </div>Verbenas and Hermetics?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Several <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sons_of_Ether\" target=\"_blank\">Sons of Ether</a> leant their scientific knowledge to the Nazis and used their funding for their own experiments </div> </div> </div>Or SoE?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While modern <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mage_(WOD)\" target=\"_blank\">mages</a> are uncomfortable with the truth, both sides had originally large Axis supporters. Hitler's delving into occult mysteries and the State Shinto mysticism of Japan attracted numerous <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Tradition_(MTAs)\" target=\"_blank\">Traditionalists</a>, </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_War_II_(WOD)\" target=\"_blank\">Second World War</a> started and the Euthanatoi were the only Tradition to oppose the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_Reich\" target=\"_blank\">Third Reich</a> from the beginning actively assassinating mages participating in war crimes </div> </div> </div>Or any Traditions mages except Euthanatoi?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_War_II_(WOD)#Mage:_The_Ascension\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Wo..._The_Ascension</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Euthanatoi#World_War\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Euthanatoi#World_War</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Order_of_Hermes#Modern_Nights\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Or...#Modern_Nights</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> is 'let's reboot them as heroes'&quot; list </div> </div> </div>Well, you're 20 years behind the times on that. WW decided to create room for Technocratic (anti-)heroic PCs back in 1999. And even then, the Union haven't been portrayed as uncomplicated heroes except in CB: It. X (which was overcompensating for Technocracy: It. X). Come to think of it, even taking into account the years when oWoD was dead, Technocrats have been presented as PC-viable longer than they were antagonist-only.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not against painting the Union in finer shades than the cartoonish villainy of ye olde 1e and giving room for individual Technocrats for being heroes... but, well, one game line over we've got a book about playing the scions of a world-spanning, world-plundering empire of elemental supersoldiers that makes no bones about <i>empires suck</i>. </div> </div> </div>Yes. WW games don't have you playing uncomplicated good guys, which is why people are drawn to them. Even the Garou, who are fighting to save the world against the literal manifestation/source of all evil and spiritual corruption, have significant flaws. And in Exalted the Solars, i.e. the presumed &quot;main protagonist&quot; splat, are capable of great evils and were killed and sealed because they threatened to destroy the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you wanna be an Awakened Scientist, you've got, like, two entire traditions and a miscellany of them strewn throughout the others. (There's a surprising number of technomages in the Hermetics, in my eyes. Their science isn't the science the Technocracy would like, but even so...) </div> </div> </div>What if I don't want to play a retrofuturist mad scientist/pulp hero or l33t h4xx0r, or a technomage?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>With that said</i>, and so I don't seem like I'm just being negative - I'm not at all against stuff like we got in Revised, where the head honchos of the Union had their control disrupted, giving more latitude for the Earth-side personnel to look around and have their <i>&quot;are we the baddies?</i>&quot; moments. </div> </div> </div>Well, that seems to be the tone that T:R is going for. At any rate, none of the post-GTTech books save Revised ItX portrays them as unambiguously heroic, so I don't see what you're complaining about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 06-26-2020, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T18:29:10-07:00","id":1398913,"title":"","content":"Yeah.<br /> <br /> Let's not try to pretend the Traditions or even the Crafts have never had blood on their hands...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T19:52:23-07:00","id":1398928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1398761#post1398761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you have concerns about people playing or wanting to play ...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Or any Traditions mages except Euthanatoi?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_War_II_(WOD)#Mage:_The_Ascension\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Wo..._The_Ascension</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Euthanatoi#World_War\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Euthanatoi#World_War</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, that reference seems to forget that the whole mess with Voormas, the Auschwitz node and the Consanguinity of Eternal Joy would make &quot;Aliasi&quot; unable to play Euthanatoi too... A pity...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":3586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","user":"Alqamar Alaswad","date":". 06-25-2020, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T05:13:39-07:00","id":1399262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1398913#post1398913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah.<br /> <br /> Let's not try to pretend the Traditions or even the Crafts have never had blood on their hands...</div> </div> </div> </div>The traditions and the Crafts aren't running the dominant paradigm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T07:38:37-07:00","id":1399284,"title":"","content":"And that excuses them? No, I don't think so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T11:42:26-07:00","id":1399339,"title":"","content":"Haven't the Technocracy been playable since the Guide to the Technocracy was published?<br /> <br /> I'm not going to judge someone for personally deciding that they don't like the idea of a heroic Technocrat, and would prefer not to play them. That's a personal choice. But it's been an option for a very long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T12:46:32-07:00","id":1399354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1399339#post1399339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't the Technocracy been playable since the Guide to the Technocracy was published?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically even before that with <i>Tales of Magick: Dark Adventure</i> not only mentioning Technocratic PCs but having a plot hook tailor-made for them specifically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not going to judge someone for personally deciding that they don't like the idea of a heroic Technocrat, and would prefer not to play them. That's a personal choice. But it's been an option for a very long time. </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between that and expressing the hope that the new Technocracy book reverts them to their wholly negative early 1e characterisation and makes them unplayable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 07-14-2020, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T11:46:58-07:00","id":1400981,"title":"","content":"Hey, I just recently started getting back into Mage, and found out that, when I did, I had <i>just </i>missed this Kickstarter, which I definitely would have backed. Is there still a way to donate and read the manuscript?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13659-grubf","name":"grubf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T13:04:09-07:00","id":1400989,"title":"","content":"Backerkit. I don't know if that gives you access to the manuscript; but it gets you the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T00:04:54-07:00","id":1401072,"title":"","content":"As someone who doesn't really get the Technocracy, this has been an enlightening thread.<br /> <br /> One issue I have with playing them is that, as I understand it, they are all supposed to have the same paradigm... so they all, in theory, do magick in the same way.<br /> <br /> Which feels kind of restrictive to my tradition-loving heart because, well, what if I have an idea for how an effect is done but another technocrat player has a different idea? which one of us is not doing it right? It seems like technocratic PC's should have a &quot;spell list&quot; to reflect the idea that they all do it the same way.<br /> <br /> Or am I misunderstanding something about the Technocracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T00:55:55-07:00","id":1401076,"title":"","content":"The Order of Hermes has \u201cone way\u201d to do Magick. The Celestial Chorus has \u201cone way\u201d to Sing of the One. The Akashayana have \u201cone way\u201d to bring unity between body, mind, and soul. And so on: each Tradition has \u201cone way\u201d to do what they do. <br /> <br /> In a very general sense, at least. <br /> <br /> When you get to the particulars, there's a lot of room for variation within any given Tradition's Focus. In that regard, the Union isn't much different: it's composed of five Conventions, each with its own Focus that defines the \u201cone way\u201d that that Convention does what it does; and within the bounds of that Focus, there can be a considerable amount of versatility. <br /> <br /> There are two things that differentiate the Conventions from the Traditions where Focus is concerned. First, the Conventions' various Foci are complementary: they're designed to be pieces of an even larger and even more encompassing Union Focus. This mostly shows up in cross-training: according to the Book of Secrets, a Technocrat who attempts to learn from another Technocrat of a different Convention has a much easier time of it than does a Traditionist attempting to learn from another Traditionist. <br /> <br /> But second, the Union isn't content to have a strong, unified Focus within its own ranks. Its big failing is its insistence that <i>everyone </i> adopt that same Focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T06:14:41-07:00","id":1401099,"title":"","content":"I wonder, do the writers reads the feedback? In their last, collective manuscript, there's still the hugely missing re-org that should been in unit 8 as (still) promised in unit 1.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or, this being mage 20, should we expect a Book of Secrets: technocracy reloaded edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T06:38:20-07:00","id":1401102,"title":"","content":"Their last, collective manuscript was merely the various independent paths glued together. It says nothing about what changes may or may not be made post-Kickstarter. <br /> <br /> And yes, they do read the feedback. This has been shown in previous Kickstarters. It's up to them whether or not they <i>agree with</i> the feedback and act on it \u2014 we won't know <i>that</i> until the pre-release copy goes out on DrivethruRPG about a month before the finished project does \u2014 but they <i>do</i> read it. <br /> <br /> And we <i>will</i> be getting a companion book for TR; check the stretch goals. IIRC it's going to include Technomancer's Toybox II and Digital Web 3.0. I <i>don't</i> expect it to include the Technocracy's re-org, though: if that doesn't make it into TR itself, we may have to settle for a Storyteller's Vault product addressing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T01:52:58-07:00","id":1401299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1401102#post1401102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their last, collective manuscript was merely the various independent paths glued together. It says nothing about what changes may or may not be made post-Kickstarter.<br /> <br /> And yes, they do read the feedback. This has been shown in previous Kickstarters. It's up to them whether or not they <i>agree with</i> the feedback and act on it \u2014 we won't know <i>that</i> until the pre-release copy goes out on DrivethruRPG about a month before the finished project does \u2014 but they <i>do</i> read it.<br /> <br /> And we <i>will</i> be getting a companion book for TR; check the stretch goals. IIRC it's going to include Technomancer's Toybox II and Digital Web 3.0. I <i>don't</i> expect it to include the Technocracy's re-org, though: if that doesn't make it into TR itself, we may have to settle for a Storyteller's Vault product addressing it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's not a matter of agreeing with the feedback. When you affirm there'll be a section in Unit 8 on a topic within the manuscript, you engaged for this section to be present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T02:24:43-07:00","id":1401306,"title":"","content":"Reread my earlier comments about Unit 8: I'm in full agreement that what we got during the Kickstarter was woefully inadequate; and I <i>really</i> hope they take such feedback to heart and beef it up considerably. What I'm saying is that, first, the fact that the compiled manuscript isn't different from the pieces released during the Kickstarter means nothing; and second, that the final say as to what will go into the book is theirs, not ours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T11:51:02-07:00","id":1401524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1384914#post1384914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very excited about this. I was nervous based on some statements early on but my fears have been abated. This is exactly what I wanted out of this book and I can't wait to see what they say about the updates to Iteration X in particular.<br /> <br /> It sounds like we're getting more factions for some Conventions and I'm hoping that's for Iteration X and Progenitors both in particular given they were the two that needed them the most. Glad to see those groups are getting written by someone with a scientific background no less</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope they drop the bit about Iteration X being lost and depressed with the lost of the The Computer and trying to build a Computer2.0 . i do not know ware it came from it's not in the Iteration X Convention Book. Iteration X book has nothing in it about suffering because of losing the Computer or have a goal to make a new one.In fact it's just the reverse.<br /> It's just undoing what little character development they got and inconsistent with the other Convention Books","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2181-th3eviltwin","name":"th3eviltwin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T22:28:10-07:00","id":1401622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>th3eviltwin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1401524#post1401524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope they drop the bit about Iteration X being lost and depressed with the lost of the The Computer and trying to build a Computer2.0 . i do not know ware it came from it's not in the Iteration X Convention Book. Iteration X book has nothing in it about suffering because of losing the Computer or have a goal to make a new one.In fact it's just the reverse.<br /> It's just undoing what little character development they got and inconsistent with the other Convention Books</div> </div> </div> </div>The problems rising from scurrying to build The Computer 2.0 are heavily implied in the other Revised Conventionbooks. That's where it came from; Progenitors Revised Page 26, Syndicate Revised page 30, NWO revised page 38, VE Revised page 26.<br /> <br /> It's hard to tell what makes more sense - Iteration X quickly finding its bearings after loss of Autochtonia due to being such a well oiled machine, or the Convention kind of scrambling fanatically to rebuild the thing that gave them all their guidance, and literally the very name of the Convention.<br /> <br /> That said, the Technocracy Reloaded manuscript also makes it clear that Iteration X is not broken. Quite the opposite, like the well-oiled machine they are they adapted, adjusted and are back at working heavily to keep an eye on the sleeper's rapidly developing tech. At least when it comes to their activity on Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T03:32:45-07:00","id":1401651,"title":"","content":"a schism or competing factions likeProgenitors and the NWO would fit with overall theme of the union being in cold/shadow war with it's noble ideals and fascist tendencies fighting on each side. I just thought more could be done .mabye with unintended consequences,innovation and invention just for innovation and invention sake .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2181-th3eviltwin","name":"th3eviltwin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T06:57:03-07:00","id":1401675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>th3eviltwin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1401651#post1401651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a schism or competing factions likeProgenitors and the NWO would fit with overall theme of the union being in cold/shadow war with it's noble ideals and fascist tendencies fighting on each side. I just thought more could be done .mabye with unintended consequences,innovation and invention just for innovation and invention sake .</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that Revised: ItX was a *very* rose-tinted mirrorshades look at them as a reaction against Technocracy: ItX's... early 1e-ness, which ended up getting the book retconned as Traditions propaganda (TBF its status as an in-universe &quot;found document&quot; made this very easy). So I guess the authors of the other Revised CBs (which came out a decade later) felt the need to try and add a bit more ambiguity and conflict there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:13:16-07:00","id":1401762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1401675#post1401675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that Revised: ItX was a *very* rose-tinted mirrorshades look at them as a reaction against Technocracy: ItX's... early 1e-ness, which ended up getting the book retconned as Traditions propaganda (TBF its status as an in-universe &quot;found document&quot; made this very easy). So I guess the authors of the other Revised CBs (which came out a decade later) felt the need to try and add a bit more ambiguity and conflict there.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I see it is too ez to blame The Computer for ItX faults and mistakes. they very much like to see themselves as prometheus and tony stark but they are just as often both Caleb and Nathan from Ex Machina and icarus too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2181-th3eviltwin","name":"th3eviltwin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T18:30:33-07:00","id":1402893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1399354#post1399354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically even before that with <i>Tales of Magick: Dark Adventure</i> not only mentioning Technocratic PCs but having a plot hook tailor-made for them specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, even <i>Chaos Factor</i> allows for the possibility that the PCs might be a team of Technocracy agents, and that was well before GTTech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T11:50:13-07:00","id":1403854,"title":"","content":"I'm really enjoying the new/evolved take on the Technocracy, and especially the section outlining how a Union member's personal life and professional life interact. Very well thought out, and makes a lot of sense!<br /> <br /> As I was reading through the manuscript I got to the section describing some of the Procedures etc. and noticed a lot of the mechanics seem... clunky or outright wrong. I'm hoping this section is just pre-editing right now, but just in case, here are a few specific examples of feedback:<br /> <br /> * The Master\u2019s Edge (p216) \u2014 why not just use magick enhancing abilities to get an uncontested roll to reduce appropriate difficulties? Being a contested roll, even a Master would have difficulty getting much use out of this against your average NPC. A Master is likely to get 3 successes on average, the target is likely to get 1-2... leaving the Master with 1-2 successes. Spending 1 success for duration, that means a Master will /maybe/ get -1 difficulty.<br /> <br /> * All Triggers Locked (p217) \u2014 This would require Forces 3, not 2. Also arguably Matter 3 since guns are not made up of a homogenous material. It says it takes 3 turns to cast because the effects happen in stages. Is it an extended roll over the 3 turns? It would be nearly impossible to get 6 successes otherwise. But the way it\u2019s described, a different part of the effect happens on each turn, so... on turn 1 do all guns come out of people\u2019s hands and come to the user with a single success, or does it take 2+ to do that?<br /> <br /> * Pre-designed Proficiency Packages (p222) has variable Enlightenment, Primal Energy, and Background Cost. Nowhere does it list how much it actually costs for each variant though \u2014 are the only versions available the 3 pt (minimum of all) and 12 or (maximum of all) versions?<br /> <br /> * Zipper Ties (p223) \u2014 Why are these one-use? For something made of Primium you\u2019d think that the Union could design some way to take them off without destroying them. I see the note about recycling the materials, but that still doesn't explain why they can't just make a non-destructive version of these.<br /> <br /> * Pocket Drone (p225) \u2014 the Forces 5 Adjustment says that it can deliver damage, but doesn\u2019t mention mechanics for that. The device itself has no Enlightenment, so would that then use the user's Enlightenment instead? The Mind 2 variant says it decreases the possibility of visual detection... but gives no mechanics for this.<br /> <br /> I can give other examples, but hopefully that's enough to show that this section could be made a lot better with some editing and revision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":432,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/432-mike-todd","user":"Mike Todd","date":".  Re-read M20 core, that cleared a few things up 07-21-2020, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/432-mike-todd","name":"Mike Todd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar432_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T00:26:58-07:00","id":1404536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mike Todd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1403854#post1403854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The Master\u2019s Edge (p216) \u2014 why not just use magick enhancing abilities to get an uncontested roll to reduce appropriate difficulties? Being a contested roll, even a Master would have difficulty getting much use out of this against your average NPC. A Master is likely to get 3 successes on average, the target is likely to get 1-2... leaving the Master with 1-2 successes. Spending 1 success for duration, that means a Master will /maybe/ get -1 difficulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Duration is included in the full Roll's total success result by default M20 rules, unless you want to use Damage as well - then one of the two has to get split out with extra successes. Otherwise, the Divided Successes rule from Revised is optional - under normal circumstance, targets, damage (or duration). range etc. is all based on the *total* amount of successes rolled.<br /> ( For details about 'Targets' without the Optional Divided Successes rule, see the first 'Range' paragraph on page 543..it's a bit obscured, unlike the rest. )<br /> <br /> Still, yes, using Magick Enhancing Abilities would proooobably be more useful, but also a different kind of approach - social rolls are always a bit finnicky if used against PCs instead of NPCs, as one has to be careful about making social rolls a literal replacement for mind control. Against average NPCs though? Yeah, boosting and lowering social stat roll difficulties is probably the way to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * All Triggers Locked (p217) \u2014 This would require Forces 3, not 2. Also arguably Matter 3 since guns are not made up of a homogenous material. It says it takes 3 turns to cast because the effects happen in stages. Is it an extended roll over the 3 turns? It would be nearly impossible to get 6 successes otherwise. But the way it\u2019s described, a different part of the effect happens on each turn, so... on turn 1 do all guns come out of people\u2019s hands and come to the user with a single success, or does it take 2+ to do that? </div> </div> </div>That rote is certainly special. Mostly because it is hard to figure out how most Technocrats would justify being able to pull it off - I guess certain high-level cyborgs could.<br /> I agree that Forces 2 Matter 2 is too low for this - 3/3 seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Pre-designed Proficiency Packages (p222) has variable Enlightenment, Primal Energy, and Background Cost. Nowhere does it list how much it actually costs for each variant though \u2014 are the only versions available the 3 pt (minimum of all) and 12 or (maximum of all) versions? </div> </div> </div>No, the way I read it it is a sliding scale of primal energy and background cost. But it indeed lacks a detailed explanation on how to calculate them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Zipper Ties (p223) \u2014 Why are these one-use? For something made of Primium you\u2019d think that the Union could design some way to take them off without destroying them. I see the note about recycling the materials, but that still doesn't explain why they can't just make a non-destructive version of these. </div> </div> </div>The non-single-use variant would be Primium Cuffs. I recall those being described in one of the older books.<br /> Anyways, the mechanical advantage of making them one-use is that they become Charms - they are easy to craft even with Prime 2 if you have appropriate Tass, you can make several of them at once, and the Arete roll gets done in advance - even sleepers can use them. For re-usable Primium Cuffs to do the same and stay able to be used by anybody, they'd have to be a Talisman or Device, which are much much harder and resource intensive to create.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Pocket Drone (p225) \u2014 the Forces 5 Adjustment says that it can deliver damage, but doesn\u2019t mention mechanics for that. The device itself has no Enlightenment, so would that then use the user's Enlightenment instead? The Mind 2 variant says it decreases the possibility of visual detection... but gives no mechanics for this. </div> </div> </div>Yeeeah. I presume the Drone has no Enlightenment because those Adjustments are proooobably applied to the Drone in the form of it being a Trinket - the Drone itself is not magickal (hence no enlightenment etc.), but simply a magickally modified object.<br /> <br /> Still, this overall shows my usual gripe with Wonder secions in most Mage books - they seriously need some good proofreading and less blurryness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T07:57:47-07:00","id":1404922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1391267#post1391267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That assumes the NWO is the dark heart of the Union rather than the entirety of it.<br /> <br /> But I see the issue.<br /> <br /> I don't see Unionists as scientists. I see them as a secret conspiracy bent on world conquest. They just employ scientists. Their appeal is not YAY SCIENCE (or at least only YAY SCIENCE) it is, &amp;quot;We can't do worse than your present leaders.&amp;quot; Which is a fair argument, I think.<br /> <br /> They're the Mister House ending of Fallout: New Vegas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah Mister House is like the most stereotypical $yndcete member ever.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t back the Kickstarter, because I don\u2019t have money to spare. Can someone give me a New lore rundown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T10:17:36-07:00","id":1404937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1404922#post1404922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah Mister House is like the most stereotypical $yndcete member ever.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t back the Kickstarter, because I don\u2019t have money to spare. Can someone give me a New lore rundown?</div> </div> </div> </div>The short version is the Technocracy has re-organized itself to be far less racist and overtly oppressive. They now are all about recruiting locals and trying to fix the current problems like global warming as well as the fact that the current age of ignorance, propaganda, and mass denial is MAYBBBBBBE just kind of their fault as much as the Traditions. The Technocracy gave humanity all the tools it needed to change the world and humanity has used it to prop up science-denying dictatorships. The Technocracy isn't pro-democracy but feels like it's lost control of the situation and can't really attribute it to their enemies either.<br /> <br /> The Union is simultaneously progressive in that it has no biases to race, sex, or even religion [albeit that's a narrow path to walk] but you are expected to put the Technocracy first and last in all things and not support any group you belong to because it is your only master--which actually is causing almost as many problems as overt oppression.<br /> <br /> There's two versions of the VE due to the Avatar Storm (Quantum Event) being so dramatically changing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T13:54:15-07:00","id":1404973,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's more or less the era of the new CBs (NWO, Prog, Syn and VE) as well as a reaction to... well the state of the world we're living in.<br /> <br /> Or as I imagine a far number of Technocrats would react, &quot;Oh dammit... We gave you all these nice things and the tools to raise yourselves up and this, <b><i>this</i></b> is what you do with them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Still, it does make for an <i>interesting</i> time to be a Technocrat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T16:50:32-07:00","id":1404988,"title":"","content":"Yeah the last few years in The world have been. Ugh. Put on your Fucking mask","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T18:14:39-07:00","id":1405000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1404973#post1404973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's more or less the era of the new CBs (NWO, Prog, Syn and VE) as well as a reaction to... well the state of the world we're living in.<br /> <br /> Or as I imagine a far number of Technocrats would react, &amp;quot;Oh dammit... We gave you all these nice things and the tools to raise yourselves up and this, <b><i>this</i></b> is what you do with them.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Still, it does make for an <i>interesting</i> time to be a Technocrat.</div> </div> </div> </div>What\u2019s a CB?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T18:25:30-07:00","id":1405002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1405000#post1405000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What\u2019s a CB?</div> </div> </div> </div>Convention Book. The M20 guide to the Union is less, &quot;We're good and noble people!&quot; than the Convention Books of Revised but still a lot more apologetic than I really think my games go with. It's very well written, though, and I've been using it for a current game.<br /> <br /> Some good changes:<br /> <br /> * The Five Metal Dragons are....just what the Asian Technocracy is called.<br /> * The number of Asian Technocrats outnumbers the white ones so there's no need for a &quot;conspiracy&quot; by them<br /> * They want to solve deforestation with HIT Marks<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-27-2020, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T19:06:22-07:00","id":1405004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1405002#post1405002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Convention Book. The M20 guide to the Union is less, &amp;quot;We're good and noble people!&amp;quot; than the Convention Books of Revised but still a lot more apologetic than I really think my games go with. It's very well written, though, and I've been using it for a current game.<br /> <br /> Some good changes:<br /> <br /> * The Five Metal Dragons are....just what the Asian Technocracy is called.<br /> * The number of Asian Technocrats outnumbers the white ones so there's no need for a &amp;quot;conspiracy&amp;quot; by them<br /> * They want to solve deforestation with HIT Marks</div> </div> </div> </div>Stopping deforestion with hit mark sis always appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T00:15:21-07:00","id":1405028,"title":"","content":"Aside of the overall thematics, the book also gives a lot of details about life in the Union;<br /> How an Agent past a certain lower rank reconciles a normal life with their Union life, a lot of Technocratic terms for things, how Union operations are organized and handled, what the appopriate levels of response and force are to certain things, etc.<br /> <br /> It is a REALLY good book for STs wanting to run a Union chronicle, AND a good book for players because it comes with lots of fluff and Union-everyday. It gives a way more detailed look into such things than Guide To The Technocracy did. Which is very fine, as GttT was kind of a first Big Glimpse into the Ascension War from the Union's side of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T08:55:20-07:00","id":1405353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1385218#post1385218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From various podcasts and posts it seems like Paradox isn't going to greenlight any more *20 projects for any lines. So hopefully we get a whole bunch of stretchgoals for this and hopefully Victorian Mage still goes ahead. Though Satyros has said he's looking into getting non-greenlit projects up on the Storytellers Vault just as the C20 Developers and Freelancers have done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I REALLY hope, that this is not the case because this means that we will not see anymore german translations of it. I wonder what the sense would be behind this because from my impression those are great and I doubt I would love for example VTM as much as I do now if I would have started with VTMV instead of V20.<br /> <br /> Anyway, earlier there whas discussed about how the Technocracy is doing enlighted science and either my viewpoint is to much on Magic is willworking or I lack explaining but I can not really imagine the Technocrats doing science. So for me Technocracy would be like said before from someone else, either believing so much into Science that you deny doing magic or defining what would be the laws of the world like Physics or Chemistry.<br /> <br /> The last thing is what my character is believing but he stopped thinking about because to much Whataboutism confused more then leaving to answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 07-30-2020, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T15:29:11-07:00","id":1406845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1405002#post1405002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Convention Book. The M20 guide to the Union is less, &quot;We're good and noble people!&quot; than the Convention Books of Revised but still a lot more apologetic than I really think my games go with. It's very well written, though, and I've been using it for a current game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, apart from ItX none of the Revised CBs really go with &quot;we're wholeheartedly noble and good!&quot;<br /> <br /> NWO has the Atlas Project and the rest of the usual shenanigans ...<br /> Progenitors are the most militantly anti-Traditionalist and largely want to restart the Pogrom<br /> Syndicate ... eh, doesn't have *that* much bad stuff going on, but they still take blank cheques from Pentex, no questions asked.<br /> Void Engineers have become the most authoritarian, militaristic Convention and are secretly keeping the Avatar Storm going.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T16:10:08-07:00","id":1406854,"title":"","content":"Wait, what? Where did you get \u201cand are secretly keeping the Avatar Storm going\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinit