ews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T20:56:54-07:00","id":1446902,"title":"","content":"Joking aside, what are the thoughts of people with the backer's copy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T21:13:11-07:00","id":1446905,"title":"","content":"For starters...the &quot;splat&quot; artwork for the Conventions is MUCH better then the one in M20 core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T23:35:03-07:00","id":1446919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1406900#post1406900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kind of. The Avatar Storm was presented in the Void Engineers Convention Book as the main thing that was holding Threat Null at bay; remove the Storm, and you need a different justification as to why Threat Null isn't invading the Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>well they\u2019re Spirits, so it\u2019s not like invading the material world is super easy (if it were, Banes would have done it in mass a long time ago)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T23:38:25-07:00","id":1446920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1446902#post1446902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Joking aside, what are the thoughts of people with the backer's copy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like a lot of it. There are a few points where I think they over corrected, and the authority well intentioned agents are operating under could stand to be a tad darker. The Union at my own table will probably land somewhere between the original Guide to the Technocracy and this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T22:55:59-07:00","id":1447527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1446902#post1446902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Joking aside, what are the thoughts of people with the backer's copy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have made the Union more dark and villainous but I think this version is a better version of the playable Union than the Revised Conventions books. The best way to get past the &quot;conspiracy theorist's wet dream&quot; issues is to just make them good guys or at least no more or less antiheroes than the Traditions, I suppose.<br /> <br /> The M20 Technocracy is certainly closer to that than the reverse.<br /> <br /> I do wish we had more resources on Threat Null, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-05-2021, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T10:08:09-07:00","id":1447596,"title":"","content":"As I use the Union it represents the paradigm of the enlightenment as corrupted by imperialism (which is historically what happened), so it\u2019s actively antagonistic as it needs to be but also worth fighting to save for Technocratic games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-05-2021, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T10:38:41-07:00","id":1447597,"title":"","content":"I draw a distinction between the Practices of Enlightened Science and the Paradigms of the Technocracy. To that end, I make sure that there are plenty of Enlightened Scientists in my setting who <i>aren't</i> Technocrats \u2014 in part by following the advice in <b>Mage Made Easy</b> about <i>not</i> shoving everything into the framework of the Ascension War, and in part by making use of the Navalon metaplot to provide an Ascension War faction that uses the Practices of Enlightened Science without the Paradigms of the Union. (And I must say that it's so much easier for me to play the technocracy as straight up villains when they don't hold a monopoly on science and technology.)<br /> <br /> As such, a lot of what I use Technocracy Reloaded for is as source material for non-technocrats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-05-2021, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T11:38:40-07:00","id":1447607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384442-m20-technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-discussion?p=1447597#post1447597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I draw a distinction between the Practices of Enlightened Science and the Paradigms of the Technocracy. To that end, I make sure that there are plenty of Enlightened Scientists in my setting who <i>aren't</i> Technocrats \u2014 in part by following the advice in <b>Mage Made Easy</b> about <i>not</i> shoving everything into the framework of the Ascension War, and in part by making use of the Navalon metaplot to provide an Ascension War faction that uses the Practices of Enlightened Science without the Paradigms of the Union. (And I must say that it's so much easier for me to play the technocracy as straight up villains when they don't hold a monopoly on science and technology.)<br /> <br /> As such, a lot of what I use Technocracy Reloaded for is as source material for non-technocrats.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just emphasize that Enlightened Scientists who resist the Union's authoritarian agenda are welcomed in the Virtual Adept and the Society of Ether even if they don't indulge the less consistent with mainstream scientific consensus aspects of those Traditions. It's just safer to make sure you're part of a stronger faction because an Orphan Enlightened Scientist is very vulnerable to conscription by the Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T12:44:00-07:00","id":1447613,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I used to do it that way too. And I do still include some Enlightened Scientists in the ranks of the Society of Ether and Virtual Adepts. But I rather like the Mage Made Easy notion that Mage doesn't <i>have</i> to be about the Ascension War; and even if it is, Mages are potent enough individually that they aren't that susceptible to force recruitment. In particular, enlightened scientists aren't any more susceptible to recruitment then orphan Mages are. And the latter can get by reasonably well without having to join up with some other faction for safety.<br /> <br /> Granted, a truly lone mage is comparatively vulnerable. But that's not a matter of factions so much as it is a matter of not having any friends. And how often does <i>that</i> happen in a role-playing group? Conversely, joining a faction theoretically has safety benefits; but in practice, Mages tend to rely more on their Chantry than on their factions. And unless you <i>choose</i> to play up the \u201cbehind the eight ball\u201d style of Orphan, there's no reason why a Chantry can't be populated in part or even in whole by independent Mages. <br /> <br /> Plus, it's possible to have a support network beyond your local Chantry without it having to be one of the Awakened factions. If you don't want to make up your own, which is always an option (see the numerous fictional organizations that exist in shows such as Knight rider, macgyver, the 6 million dollar man, and so on), you can raid other game lines for ideas. If you're operating in the East, for example, there's no reason why your Enlightened cyborg can't be a member of Task Force Zero. <br /> <br /> And again, I use the Navalon metaplot for those Mages who <i>do</i> prefer or need safety in numbers and don't want to be stuck in the Traditions. <br /> <br /> That's what it means to downplay the Ascension War: there are more choices than Technocracy, Traditions, or Disparates. And I greatly prefer the greater diversity of options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T10:49:47-07:00","id":1449359,"title":"","content":"*continues reading*<br /> <br /> .....whhhyyyyy the fuck does the Syndicate Focus write-ups include nephandic Focus elements from BotF? And ONLY the Syndicate (expanded) splat write-ups?<br /> <br /> Consistency issues aside, between this and VM, we're right back to apparently no one following Brucato's intended intent of &quot;BotF is NOT a Player's Guide&quot;.<br /> <br /> (yes yes, I know BotF arguably doesn't hold to that intent as well in execution, but that's not the point)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}